ed projects. \nPresently following 6 new line projects are facing major hurdles in North \nEastern Region on account of various clea rances, land acquisition, law and \norder issues: \n(i) Sivok-Rangpo,  \n(ii) Byrnihat-Shillong,  \n(iii) Dimapur-Kohima,  \n(iv) Agartala-Akhaura, \n(v) New Moynaguri-Jogighopa, \n(vi) Teteliya-Byrnihat. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |142", "t": "Digital Payment Systems", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.142 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nDPA IN FOREIGN COUNTRIES \n \n142.  SHRI KESINENI NANI:  \n  SHRIMATI NEELAM SONKER: \n \n Will the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of projects undertaken by the Development \nPartnership Administration in foreign countries in the past \nthree years; \n \n(b) the status of the development projects and the funds allocated \nto each project; \n \n(c) the efficiency of fund utilisation by the department; \n \n(d) the priority areas for this development; and \n \n(e) the details of percent of development aid given to other \ncountries? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n[GEN. (DR) V. K. SINGH (RETD)] \n \n(a) to (c) & (e)  The list of the projects (ongoing and completed) \nundertaken by Development Partnership Administration (DPA) in \nforeign countries for the past 3 years along with the expenditure \nincurred on each project is given in the attached statement \n(Annexure). The fun ds made available for these projects have been \nutilised to the extent possible, keeping in mind local conditions in \nforeign countries.  \n \n(d)  The areas of development partnership are driven by the \npriorities of the partner country. The main areas of develo pment \npartnership undertaken with partner countries have been in the \nsectors of infrastructure, connectivity, power, healthcare, \nagriculture, Information Technology and capacity building. \n