l-Tamar, Ranchi. \n2014-15 Bauxite Garha-Hanrup-Kabrapat-Risahatolli-Kurhetola \nBlock, Gumla. \n55.93 \nMT \n \n \n \nMeghalaya \n2012-13 Limestone Umphyrluh Block. Jaintia Hills  1041.91 \nMT 2013-14 Limestone Umphyrluh Block. Jaintia Hills  \n2013-14 Limestone North of Larket Block. Jaintia Hills  \n2014-15 Limestone North Larket block,Litang Valley,Vill-\nKhliehriat,East, Jaintia-Hills, \n2014-15 Limestone Mawalong- Ishamati Block, Shora taluka, East Khasi \nHills  \n2014-15 Bauxite Maopatshiyar Block, Rambrai area, Nongstoin \nTaluka, West Khasi Hills  \n2 MT \n \n \n \n \nArunachal Pradesh \n2013-14 Limestone Daba Gamlin area.West Siang 0.52 \nMT \n2014-15 Iron ore Jaiyor-Yomgum Block, (villages Yomcha, Yomgum, \nGamkak and Laggi- Gamlin), Yomcha Sub Division, \nWest Siang  \n0.026 \nMT \n2014-15 Copper Ningcho Block,  Pijirang Circle, Seppa, East Kameng  0.01 \nMT \n2014-15 Graphite Tai Block, Tai- Tachidoni, Tirbin Taluka, West Siang  0.19 \nMT \n \nUttar Pradesh \n2013-14 Andalusite Salaidih Harwariya Mahakoshal Group, \nSonbhadra  \n31.90 \nMT \n2014-15 Andalusite Banwarjharia Block,Maripur area, Taluka- Dhubi, \nSonbhadra. \n2014-15"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |292", "t": "Micro Water Conservation Projects", "head": "O.I.H.\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE, \nCOOPERATION\n \n& FARMERS WELFARE\n \n \n��������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������\n��\n������\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE \n6\nTH\n \nDECEMBER, 2016\n \n \n��\n������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n \n*292.\n \n \nDR. BANSHILAL MAHATO: \n \n \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS \nWELFARE   \n \n��������\n��\n������\n��\n����������\n��\n����������\n��\n½ãâ¨ããè\n  \n \nbe pleased to state\n:\n \n \n(a) \n \nthe status of Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana\n, along with targets fixed and \nthe achievements made in, both physical and financial terms; \n \n \n(b) \n \nwhether the implementation of the micro water conservation projects especially \nthose facing water shortage has brought about a transformation in the living s\ntandards of \nrural people and if so, the details thereof; and \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether the Government has any proposal to promote water conservation in the \nareas facing water scarcity in the country and if so, the details thereof and the manner in \nwhich the farmers a\nre likely to be benefited through these projects?\n \n������������\n��\nMINISTER OF AGRICULTURE\n \nAND FARMERS WELFARE\n \n��������\n��\n������\n��\n����������\n��\n����������\n  \n��������������\n��\n \n \n \n  \n(SHRI RADHA MOHAN SINGH\n)\n \n \n \n(a) to (c\n):\n \nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n��\n��\n��\n\n�������������������� ������������������ ������ ������\n������������ ������ ������������ �������� ������ ��\n��\n���� ������ ��\n������ ������������\n����������������������������������������\n��\n������\n��������\n��������������������������������\n��\n��\n����\n��\n����������������������������\n��\n��\n \n(\na) to (c)\n:\n \nPradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchayee Yojana (PMKSY) has been \noperationalised\n \nfrom 1st July, 2015 with the objective of enhancing irrigation coverage \nand improving the delivery system at farm level.    The programme aims at end\n-\nto end \nsolutions in irrigation supply chain, viz. water sources, distribution network and farm \nlevel appl\nications.   An area of 13.5 lakh hectare for creation of irrigation potential and \n15 lakh hectare for coverage under command area development has been targeted \nduring the period of 2015\n-\n16 to 2019\n-\n20 under PMKSY.  Besides, creation of protective \nirrigation\n \nin  11.5 lakh hectare through watershed development projects and coverage of \n10 million hectares under precision irrigation have been envisaged under the \nprogramme.  An amount of Rs. 50,000 crore as central share has been earmarked for \nimplementation of t\nhe programme.  \n \n \n \nDuring the year 2015\n-\n16, a target of 1.2 lakh hectare under Accelerated Irrigation \nBenefit Programme (AIBP), 0.3 lakh hectare for surface minor irrigation, 2 lakh hectare \nunder command area development,  2.5 lakh hectare under groundwater\n \ndevelopment, \n0.2 lakh hectare under repair restoration and renovation of water bodies, 4.4 lakh \nprotective irrigation through water shed development and 5 lakh hectare under precision \nirrigation was set under the programme.   The amount released during 20\n15\n-\n16 by the \ndifferent ministries/departments for implementation of PMKSY is given at \n����������������\n��\n��\n.  \nThe state\n-\nwise achievement under various interventions of PMKSY during 2015\n-\n16 is \ngiven at \n����������������\n��\n������\n \n \n \nContd…2/\n-\n \n \n \n \n\n \n-\n2\n-\n \n \nAvailability of irrigation not o\nnly minimises the risk of drought but also helps \nfarmers to get additional income due to the scope of growing more than one \ncrop/cropping systems from the same land.  As per available report, the cropping \nintensity in irrigated area is about 1.4. \n \n \nThe Uni\non Cabinet in its meeting held on 27\nth\n \nJuly, 2016 has taken a decision to \ncomplete the ongoing 99 major and medium irrigation projects in mission mode by the \nend of December, 2019.  \nThe mission targets bringing \nadditional 76.03 lakh\n \nhectare \nunder assured irrigation.  To achieve this a dedicated long term irrigation fund is being \ncreated in NABARD with an initial corpus of about Rs. 20000 crore. 23 large and \nmedium irrigation projects have been targeted for completion in 2016\n-\n17.\n \n \n \n\n����������������\n��\n����\n��\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��\n������������������������������\n��\nRs. in lakh\n \n������������\n��\n��������������������\n��\n������������������������\n��\n������������\n��\n����������\n��\nAndhra Pradesh\n \n0\n \n8787\n \n20647\n \n29434\n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n4553\n \n1800\n \n260\n \n6613\n \nAssam\n \n27165\n \n4670\n \n503\n \n32339\n \nBihar\n \n5562\n \n500\n \n2860\n \n8922\n \nChhattisgarh\n \n3277\n \n2107\n \n2030\n \n7414\n \nGoa\n \n0\n \n0\n \n30\n \n30\n \nGujarat\n \n48272\n \n10000\n \n21305\n \n79577\n \nHaryana\n \n7739\n \n691\n \n3497\n \n11926\n \nHP\n \n167\n \n2000\n \n760\n \n2928\n \nJ&K\n \n14601\n \n0\n \n487\n \n15088\n \nJharkhand\n \n28162\n \n"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |293", "t": "Green India Mission", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n (DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.293 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \nDevelopment of Sports \n293. SHRI BHAGWANTH KHUBA:  \n Will the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS ; be pleased to \nstate:  \n(a)  the measures taken/being taken by the Government to develop \nthe sports and sports institutions including Sports Authority of India \n(SAI) in the country;  \n(b)  the details of funds provided by the Union Government to various \nStates/UTs for development of sports/infrastructure during each of the \nlast three years and the current year, State/UT-wise;  \n(c)  whether the Government proposes to set up any indoor sports \nstadiums across the country including Karnataka; and  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof ? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) FOR YOUTH AFFAIRS \nAND SPORTS \n(SHRI VIJAY GOEL) \n \n(a)     Development of sports and sports institutions under the Ministry \nof Youth Affairs & Sports is an on -going process.  Measures are taken  \nfrom time to time for this purpose.  Major steps taken recently are \nformulation of ‘Khelo India’  programme  which, inter-alia, provides  for \n\nholding of annual sports competitions, sports talent identification and \nc