������ ������� ���� ���������� ������������� ���� ����� ���� ������ ��������� ����\n\n� � � � � � �\n� �\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������������������������������\n�\n� ������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������\n�\n� ��� ���� ���� ����� ��������� ������������ ������� ����� ������� ���� ������ ��������\n������� ���������� ����������� ������� ������������ ��� ��������� ���� ������ ��� ��������\n������������ ���� ���� ��������� ���������� ��������������� ������� ������� ��� ���� ������� ���\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������\n� � �\n�\n� � � � � � �������\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n\n� � � � � � �\n� �\nAnnexure-I \n� �\n���� � ������\n�������������\n����������������\n��������������\n������������\n��������\n����������\n����\n���������\n��������\n�����������\n��������\n����������\n���������\n�� ��� � �� ��� � �����������\n�� ���������� ��� ��� � �����������\n�� ������������� ��� ��� � �����������\n�� ������ � ��� ��� � �����������\n�� �������������� � ��� ��� � �����������\n�� ��������� � ��� ��� � �����������\n�� ���������� ��� ��� � �����������\n�� ��������� � ��� ��� � �����������\n�� �������������� � ��� ��� � �����������\n��� �������� ��� ��� � �����������\n��� ������������ ��� ��� � �����������\n��� ��������� � �� �� � ������\n������� ��� � �� ��\n� � � � �\n� � �\n��������������������������\n�"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |389", "t": "Rashtriya Rail Sanraksha Kosh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.389 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 14.12.2016 \n \nRASHTRIYA RAIL SANRAKSHA KOSH \n \n*389.  SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT: \n SHRI B. SRIRAMULU:  \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Railways has proposed creation of the Rashtriya Rail \nSanrakha Kosh (RRSK) with a view to give additional emphasis on the \nsafety and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) whether the Ministry of Finance has given its approval for the creation of \nthe said kosh; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and further action taken by the Government in \nthis regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS \n \n \n(SHRI SURESH PRABHAKAR PRABHU) \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 389 BY SHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT & SHRI B. SRIRAMULU TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 14.12.2016 REGARDING RASHTRIYA RAIL \nSANRAKSHA KOSH \n \n(a) Yes, Madam. Ministry of Railways has proposed to create a non-lapsible \n“Rastriya Rail Sanraksha Kosh” (RRSK) totaling ì 1,19,183 Crores, out of \nwhich ì 1,11,683 Crores to be funded by Ministry of Finance for safety \nimprovement of Indian Railways. The safety related works identified \nwith approximate fund requirement are as under:   \nSN Item Approx. Fund  \n(ì  in Cr.) \n1.  Track Works 30032 \n2.  Bridge Rehabilitation Works 3250 \n3.  Other safety works for Track Vehicular \nUltrasonic testing system for Rail/Welds etc. \n11697 \n4.  Safety Works at Level Crossing (Elimination of \nLC, ROB/RUB/Subway etc.) \n43444 \n5.  S&T replacement and improvement works 10140 \n6.  Rolling Stock replacement and improvement \nworks \n9263.55 \n7.  OHE replacement and other electrical \nimprovement work \n9495 \n8.  Human Resource Development 1861.45 \n Grand Total 1,19,183 \n \n \n-2- \n\n(b) & (c) Hon’ble Finance Minister has agreed to constitute the fund subject \nto conditions that 75% of the total requirement should be financed  by \nMinistry of Railways through resource mobilization and balance 25% of the \nrequirement will be provided out of the Gross Budgetary Support (GBS) \nmade available by General Revenues over a period of 5 years. The matter is \nbeing pursued with Ministry of Finance.  \n \n***** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |39", "t": "Open Defecation Free States", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.  * 39 (19th  Position)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17-11-2016  \n \nOpen Defecation Free States \n \n*39. SHRI MULLAPPALLY RAMACHANDRAN: \n \nWill the Minister of DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of States which have been declared as Open Defecation Free States; and \n \n(b) whether the Government has reviewed the progress in other States in this regard and if so, the \ndetails thereof and the State-wise details of sanitation coverage? \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF DRINKING WATER AND SANITATION  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n \n(a) to (b) A Statement is laid on the table of the House.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.  *39 for 17.11.2016. \n \n \n(a) Sikkim, Himachal Pradesh and Kerala have been declared as Open Defecation Free (ODF) \nStates. \n \n(b) Ministry of Drinking Water and Sanitation regularly review s the SBM(G) programme. \nThere is \na spurt in the progress made under the programme. Against the e xpected outcome of 50 lakh  for \nindividual latrines for the year 2014-15, 58,54,987  latrines were constructed, which is an \nachievement of 117%  of the target. During 2015-16, 127.41 lakh  toilets have already been \nconstructed against the target of 120.00 lakh . For the year 2016-17 , against the expected outcome \nof 1.5 crore  individual latrines, 90,61,950  individual latrines (60.41%)  have been constructed as on \n12-11-2016.  Since the launch of Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin) on 2 nd  October, 2014, 267.51 \nlakh  toilets have already been constructed under SBM(G) as on 12.11.2016. Sanitation Coverage, \nwhich was 42.01% on 2.10.2014 , has increased to 56.76% on 12.11.2016 . State/UT-wise \nSanitation Coverage in rural areas is at Annexure-1.  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nAnnexure-1 \nStatement referred in part (b) of the reply to Lok Sabha Starred Question No.39 due for reply \non 17-11-2016 \n \nState/UT-wise Sanitation Coverage in rural areas as on 12-11-2016  \n   \nS.N.  STATE/UT Rural Sanitation Coverage as \non 12.11.2016 \n1 A & N ILANDS 55.83 \n2 ANDHRA PRADESH 48.76 \n3 ARUNACHAL PRADESH 73.31 \n4 ASSAM 58.75 \n5 BIHAR 25.44 \n6 CHHATTISGARH 63.24 \n7 GOA 76.08 \n8 GUJARAT 83.56 \n9 HARYANA 87.55 \n10 HIMACHAL PRADESH 100.26 \n11 JAMMU & KASHMIR 34.96 \n12 JHARKHAND 43.02 \n13 KARNATAKA 60.95 \n14 KERALA 100.04 \n15 MADHYA PRADESH 47.85 \n16 MAHARASHTRA 68.85 \n17 MANIPUR 83.07 \n18 MEGHALAYA 84.89 \n19 MIZORAM 85.12 \n20 NAGALAND 66.75 \n21 ODISHA 35.69 \n22 PUDUCHERRY 51.16 \n23 PUNJAB 79.60 \n24 RAJASTHAN 65.51 \n25 SIKKIM 99.90 \n26 TAMIL NADU 65.11 \n27 TELANGANA 44.29 \n28 TRIPURA 76.02 \n29 UTTAR PRADESH 45.04 \n30 UTTARAKHAND 93.04 \n31 WEST BENGAL 81.09 \n  All India  56.76 \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |390", "t": "Viewership of DD Kisan", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 390 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \nSHORTAGE OF OFFICIALS IN PANCHAYATS \n \n†390 SHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL: \n  \n Will the Minister of PANCHAYATI RAJ be pleased to state: \n \n(a) Whether there is shortage of officers/employees at Panchayat, Block Samiti and Zila \nParishad level in States including Uttar Pradesh; \n(b) if so, the details thereof, State/ UT-wise; \n(c) whether there is shortage of basic infrastructure like office, compute risation of \nPanchayats and training of various representatives/ officers of Panchayati Raj to meet the \nneeds of all Gram Panchayats; and \n(d) if so, the details thereof and the amount allocated and utilised during the last three years? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF PANCHAYATI RAJ \n \n(SHRI PARSHOTTAM RUPALA) \n \n(a) to (d) Yes , Madam. As per the information received from State s/UTs, there is a \nshortage of staff, basic infrastructure viz office buildings and computers at each level of \nPanchayats; and there exist gaps in the capacities of elected representatives and functionaries \nof Panchayats in most of the States/UTs including Uttar Pradesh to be able to discharge their \nfunctions properly. ‘Panchayat’ being a State subject, the primary responsibility for providing \nsuch facilities vest s with the States. The details of officers/employees and infrastructure in \nPanchayats are not maintained by the Ministry of Panchayati Raj. \n \nThe Ministry of Panchayati Raj has been augmenting the efforts of the States under \nthe Rashtriya Gram Swaraj Abhiyan [erstwhile Rajiv Gandhi Panchayat Sashaktikaran \nAbhiyan (RGPSA)] scheme. The financial and technical support has been provided to States \nfor strengthening Panchayats including for administrative and technical support, co nstruction \nand maintenance of Gram Panchayat buildings, computers and training and  capacity building \nof various stakeholders of Panchayats. With effect from the financial year 2015-16, the \nsupport for administrative and technical items, construction and maintenance of Gram \nPanchayat buildings, and computers has been discontinued.  \n  \nThe funds were also provided under district component of the Backward Regions \nGrant Fund Programme (BRGF) for supplementing and converging existing developmental \ninflows into identified backward districts so as to bridge critical gaps in local infrastructure \nand other development requirements. With effect from the financial year 2015 -16, the BRGF \nhas been delinked from the budgetary support of the Central Government. \n \nThe details of funds released and utilised by States/ UTs are given at Annexe I and II. \n \n**** \n \n\n \nAnnexe I \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to Part (a) to (d) of Lok Sabha unstarred Question No -390 regarding \nShortage of Officials in Panchayats to be answered on 17.11.2016. \n \nStatus regarding State -wise Funds Released & Funds utilized under RGPSA/RGSA during 2013 -14 to \n2016-17 \n            (Rs. in crores) \nS.No. Name of the \nState/ UTs \n2013-14 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \nFunds \nRelease\nd  \nFunds \nUtilized*    \nFunds \nReleased  \nFunds \nUtilized*  \nFunds \nReleased                       \nFunds \nUtilized*   \nFunds \nRelease\nd                       \nFunds \nUtilized \n* * \n1 Assam 16.65 16.65 26.04 26.04 17.08 11.66 21.83   \n2 Andhra \nPradesh 41.6 41.6 24.19 24.19 12.5 10.6 45.8   \n3 Arunachal \nPradesh 8.71 8.71 7.72 7.28 0       \n4 Bihar 8.61 0 63.67 0 0       \n5 Chhattisgarh 25.73 25.73 11.4 11.4 14.64 10.72 21.31   \n6 Gujarat 31.65 31.65 1.06 1.06 0   33.38   \n7 Haryana 2.93 2.93 18.78 6.25 0       \n8 Himachal \nPradesh 15.84 15.84 15.26 7.78 2.48       \n9 Jammu & \nKashmir 9.45 0 8.58 0 0       \n10 Jharkhand 16.45 15.83 16.2 14.36 9.49   20.9   \n11 Karnataka 25.56 25.56 46.8 46.74 32.71 0     \n12 Kerala 16.58 16.58 14.49 11.28 0   8.55   \n13 Manipur 1.6 1.6 5.42 5.42 5.4 5.4 4.81 4.81 \n14 Madhya \nPradesh 42.83 42.83 37.46 0 10.8 9.52 41.83   \n15 Maharashtra 83.17 83.17 34.76 34.76 4.5 2.84 21.17   \n16 Odisha 28.73 28.73 32.92 32.92 0   20.01   \n17 Punjab 7.97 7.97 0 0 2.69 2.69 7   \n18 Rajasthan 15.45 15.45 11.56 11.56 4.48 3.88 22.27   \n19 Sikkim 3.15 3.15 6.85 6.85 1.26 1.19 2.33   \n20 Tamil Nadu 58.14 58.08 20.16 20.16 8.96 8.05 27.32   \n21 Tripura 9.09 9.09 2.36 2.08 1.35 0 5.3   \n22 Telangana 34.64 34.64 29.94 29.94 13.13 9.23 14.48   \n23 Uttarkhand 5.47 5.47 13.04 13.04 3.09 2.58 13.21   \n24 Uttar \nPradesh 42.37 33.85 0 0 11   39.87   \n25 West Bengal 8.23 8.23 27.71 27.71 9.91 9.17 21.85   \n26 Mizoram 0 0 2.48 2.48 0   6.22   \n27 Dadra 0 0 1.09