�������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������������������������\n�\n���� �����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�����������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������ �\n����� � � � � � � � � � ������������\n����� �����������\n����������\n��������������������������\n���������������������\n������\n�������� ��� ���� ����\n�������� ���� ���� ����\n�������� ���� ���� ����\n���������\n����������������\n��� ���� ����\n�\n���������"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |53", "t": "Juvenile Homes", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 53 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF RAILWAY LINES \n \n53. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH: \n  \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has proposed any significant projects towards the \ndevelopment of railway lines in the north-eastern States of the country; and \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the estimated costs and timeline for \ncompletion of the project? \n \nANSWER \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) & (b):    For development of R ailway lines network  in North Eastern States, 20 \nmajor R ailway projects consisting of 13 new lines, 2 gauge conversions and 5 \ndoublings having aggregate length of 2624 km at a  cost of  `52030 crore have \nbeen taken up.  An expenditure of `21336 crore has been incurred on these \nprojects upto March, 2016.  An outlay of `5040 crore has been provided for 2016 -\n17 for these projects and residual liabilities of some completed projects. \n Completion of projects depends on many factors such as availability of \nfunds, land acquisition, forestry and  wild life clearances, shifting of services, \nconstruction of road over and road under bridges by road maintaining agencies \netc. As many of these f actors are not within the control of Railways, it is not \nfeasible to fix timelines for all the projects.  However, Railways have taken \nvarious measures to expedite completion of projects including substantial \nincrease in allocation of funds, prioritization  of projects, delegation of powers at \nfield level, inviting the State Governments to participate with Railways for \nresource mobilization for projects, nomination of nodal officers for improved co -\nordination with the State Governments etc. \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |54", "t": "Use of Banned/Spurious Drugs", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 54\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016\nUSE OF BANNED/SPURIOUS DRUGS\n†*54. SHRI HARI MANJHI:\nSHRI KANWAR SINGH TANWAR:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether there are reports that a number of patients have lost their lives due to\nadministration of wrong, spurious and expired drugs by the doct ors in various\nGovernment and Corporate Hospitals and if so, the details thereof and action taken\nthereon;\n(b) whether the Government has taken note of the fact that medicines are being sold\nonline and offline without proper prescription by the doctors inducing the chances of\ndrug abuse and if so, the details thereof and preventive steps taken in this regard;\n(c) whether the sale of spurious and expired drugs is going on unabated in small\ntowns and villages especially in remote and far -flung areas of th e country and if so,\nthe details thereof;\n(d) whether bar coding for medicines, training for drug manufacturers and zero\ntolerance towards sub -standard medicines is a matter of grave concern for the\nGovernment and if so, the steps taken by the Government to protect the consumer\nfrom counterf eit/sub-standard drugs being sold online and to regulate the\ne-pharmacy web business; and\n(e) the details of drug testing laboratories and new laboratories proposed to be set\nup, State/UT-wise.\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 54* FOR 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016\n(a): Stray incidents of this nature get reported in the media from time to time.\nThese are investigated by the Central and the State Governments and necessary\nremedial action is taken.\n(b): Sale and distribution of drugs in the country is regulated under the provisions\nof the Drugs & Cosmetics Act, 1940 and Rules thereunder. In accordance with these\nRules, drugs specified in Schedules H, H1 and X cannot be sold except on, and in\naccordance with the prescription of a Registered Medical Practitioner from a\nlicensed premise. Some instances of online sale of medicines had been r eported in\nthe media. Wherever any violation is noticed, suitable action is taken by the State\nLicensing Authorities.\n(c): No such reports of unabated sale of spurious and expired drugs in small towns\nand villages of the country has come to the notice of the Central Government.\nHowever, a few stray incidents are reported from time to time and action as per\nprovisions of the law is taken in such cases.\n(d): The Government is committed to ensuring that the quality, safety and efficacy\nof drugs are not compromised. With this in view, the Government has taken a series\nof measures. These include:\n(i) stringent penalties including making certain offences cognizable and non -\nbailable;\n(ii) establishment of special designated Courts for trial of offences under Drug s\nand Cosmetics Act for speedy disposal of cases;\n(iii) announcement of a Whistle Blower Scheme to encourage vigilant public\nparticipation for detection of movement of spurious drugs in the country;\n(iv) issuance of guidelines to the State Drugs Controllers for taking action on\nsamples of drugs declared spurious, adulterated, misbranded or ‘not of standard\nquality’;\n(v) instructions to the concerned staff to keep a vigil and draw samples of drugs\nfor test and analysis for monitoring the quality of drugs moving in the country;\n(vi) increase in the number of posts in the Central Drugs Standard Control\nOrganization (CDSCO);\n\n(vii) re-equipping of drug testing laboratories with state-of-the-art equipment;\n(viii) large scale nation -wide survey to determine the ‘not of standard quality’\ndrugs;\n(ix) conducting workshops and training programmes for skill enhancement in\nareas such as Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP), Good Laboratory\nPractices (GLP), Good Distribution Pr actices (GDP), Good Clinical Practice\n(GCP) and  Good Storage and Distribution Practices (GSP) to regulators and\nindustry in partnership with other Departments, industry and regulators of other\ncountries including USA and European Union.\n(x) Conducting tra ining programmes for laboratory personnel of State and\nCentral laboratories to upgrade their analytical capabilities and skill sets.\n(xi) risk based inspections of manufacturing facilities have been started.\nBar coding has already been started for expo rts. As far as bar coding for domestic\nsupplies is concerned, a draft notification had been issued on 03.06.2015 to invite\nobjections and suggestions from the stakeholders.  The notification was, however,\nnot finalized keeping in view the reservations of m anufacturers regarding high cost\nof bar coding.\nThe issue relating to online sale of drugs has been examined by the Drug\nConsultative Committee (DCC) and a Sub -Committee of the DCC. The DCC has\nfinalised i"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |55", "t": "Income Declaration Scheme", "head": "भारत सरकार\n \n\u0000व\u0000 मं\u0000ालय\n \nराज\u0000व \u0000वभाग\n \nलोक सभा\n \nतारां\u0000कत \u0000\u0000न सं\n. \n*\n55\n \n(\nिजसका उ\u0000र शु\u0000वार\n,18 \nनव\u0000बर\n,\n \n2016\n/\n27 \nका\u0000त\u0000क\n,\n \n1938 \n(\nशक\n) \nको \u0000दया जाना है\n)\n \n \nआय घोषणा योजना\n \n*\n55. \nडॉ॰ \u0000हना \u0000वजयकुमार गावीतः\n \n    \n \nडॉ॰ कंभमप\u0000त ह\u0000रबाबूः\n \n \n\u0000या \u0000व\u0000 मं\u0000ी यह बताने क\u0000 \nकृपा कर\u0000गे \u0000कः\n \n(\nक\n) \n \n\u0000या सरकार ने आय घोषणा योजना\n, 2016\n \nक\u0000 घोषणा क\u0000 थी और य\u0000द हां\n, \nतो त\u0000संबंधी \u0000यौरा \u0000या है\n;\n \n(\nख\n) \n \nअपनी अघो\u0000षत आय क\u0000 घोषणा करने वाले \u0000यि\u0000तय\u0000 क\u0000 सं\u0000या \u0000कतनी है और नकद\u0000\n \nतथा अ\u0000य \nप\u0000रसंप\u0000\u0000य\u0000 के \u0000प म\u0000 सरकार \u0000वारा \u0000ा\u0000त क\u0000 गई कुल घो\n\u0000षत धनरा\u0000श \u0000कतनी है\n;\n \n(\nग\n) \n \nआय घोषणा योजना\n, 2016\n \nके भाग के \u0000प म\u0000 सं\u0000ह\u0000त \u0000कए गए कर क\u0000 मा\u0000ा \u0000कतनी है\n;\n \n(\nघ\n) \n \n\u0000वैि\u0000छक घोषणा योजना\n, 1997\n \nके मुकाबले आय घोषणा योजना\n, 2016\n \n\u0000कस हद तक सफल या असफल \nरह\u0000 है\n; \nऔर\n \n(\nङ\n) \n \nकाला धन को उजागर करने के \u0000लए सरकार \u0000वारा अ\u0000य \u0000या\n कदम उठाए गए ह\u0000\n/\nउठाए\n \nजा रहे ह\u0000 और \nइसके \u0000या प\u0000रणाम रहे\n?\n \n \nउ\u0000र\n \n \n\u0000व\u0000 मं\u0000ी \n(\n\u0000ी \nअ\u0000ण जेटल\u0000\n)\n \n \n(\nक\n) \nसे \n(\nङ\n)\n \nएक \u0000ववरण सभा पटल पर रख \u0000दया गया है।\n \n \n \n \n\nआय घोषणा योजना के बारे म\u0000 डॉ॰ \u0000हना \u0000वजयक ुमार गावीत\n, \nसंसद सद\u0000य\n;\n \nऔर डॉ\n॰ कंभमप\u0000त ह\u0000रबाब ू\n, \nसंसद \nसद\u0000य\n, \n\u0000वारा पूछे गए\n \nलोकसभा\n \nके\n \n\u0000दनांक \n18\n.\n11\n.\n2016 \nके\n \nतारां\u0000कत \u0000\u0000न सं\u0000या \n*\n55 \nके उ\u0000र म\u0000 \nउि\u0000ल\n\u0000खत \n\u0000ववरण \n \n \n(\nक\n)\n \n \nआय घोषणा योजना\n, \n2016 \n(\nयोजना\n)\n, \n\u0000व\u0000 अ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\n, \n2016 \nके अंतग\u0000त श ु\u0000 क\u0000 गई थी ता\u0000क ऐसे \n\u0000यि\u0000तय\u0000 को एक अवसर \u0000दया जा सके िज\u0000ह\u0000ने \u0000वगत म\u0000 प ूरे कर अदा\n \nनह\u0000ं \u0000कए ह\u0000 और वे आगे आकर इसके \nसंबंध म\u0000 अघो\u0000षत आय घो\u0000षत क\nर सक \u0000 और उस पर कर\n, \nअ\u0000धभार और शा\nि\u0000त का भुगतान कर सक \u0000 । यह योजना \n1 \nजून\n, \n2016 \nसे लागू हुई थी और \n30\n.\n09\n.\n2016 \nको बंद हो गई थी। \n \n \nइस योजना म\u0000\n,\n \nइस \u0000कार घो\u0000षत क\u0000 गई आय पर \n30\n% \nक\u0000 दर से कर लगाए जाने तथा\n \nदेय कर पर \n25\n \n%\n \nक\u0000 \nदर से \nअ\u0000धभार\n \n(\nिजसे कृ\u0000ष क\u0000याण उपकर कहा गया\n) \nलगाए जाने तथा देय कर पर \n25\n \n% \n \nक\u0000 दर से शा\nि\u0000त \nलगाए जाने का \u0000ावधान था। यह योजना उन \u0000यि\u0000तय\u0000 के संबंध म\u0000 उपल\u0000ध नह\u0000ं थी िजन पर \u0000व\u0000न\u0000द\u0000\u0000ट \nअ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\u0000 के अंतग\u0000त\n, \nइस योजना के तहत \u0000व\u0000न\u0000द\u0000\n\u0000ट \n\u0000कए अनुसार काय\u0000वा\u0000हयाँ लं\n\u0000ब\nत थीं।\n \n \n(\nख\n)\n \nइस योजना के अंतग\u0000त \n*\n64\n,\n275 \nघोषणाकता\u0000ओं ने \n*\n65\n,\n250 \n\u0000पए क\u0000 अघो\u0000षत आय क\u0000 घोषणा क\u0000 है।\n \n*\nअनं\u0000तम\n \n \n(\nग\n)\n \nइस योजना के अंतग\u0000त कर\n, \nअ\u0000धभार और शाि\u0000त\n, \n3 \n\u0000क\u0000त\u0000 म\u0000 देय है। पहल\u0000 \u0000क\u0000त के भ ुगतान क\u0000 \nअ\u0000धसू\u0000चत तार\u0000ख \n30 \nनव\u0000बर\n, \n201\n6 \nहै\n, \nअतः योजना के \u0000ह\u0000से के \u0000प म\u0000 सं\u0000\u0000हत कर क\u0000 मा\u0000ा का इस \u0000तर पर \nअनुमान नह\u0000ं लगाया जा सकता है।\n \n \n(\nघ\n)\n \nआय घोषणा योजना\n, \n2016 \n(\nआईडीएस \n2016\n) \nऔर आय का \u0000वैि\u0000छक \u0000कट\u0000करण योजना\n, \n1997 \n(\nवीडीआईएस \n1997\n) \nके तुलना\u0000मक आँकड़\u0000 नीचे सारणी म\u0000 \u0000दए गए ह\u0000\n:\n \n \nवीडीआईए\nस \n1997\n*\n \nआईडीएस \n2016\n \nघोषणाकता\u0000ओं क\u0000 सं\u0000या\n \n4\n,\n72\n,\n162\n \n64\n,\n275\n#\n \nघो\u0000षत धनरा\u0000श\n \n33\n,\n697\n.\n32 \nकरोड़\n \n65\n,\n250\n \nकरोड़\n#\n \nयोजना के अंतग\u0000त अदा \u0000कया गया\n/ \nदेय कर\n \n9\n,\n729\n.\n02 \nकरोड़\n \n29\n,\n362.5 \nकरोड़\n**\n \n \n \n*\nआंकड़\u0000 का \u0000ोतः \n2005 \nक\u0000 सीएजी \u0000रपोट\u0000 सं\u0000या \n12\n(\n\u0000\u0000य\u0000 कर\n) \n \n#\nअनं\u0000तम\n \n**\nइस योजना के अंतग\u0000त घो\u0000षत धनरा\u0000श पर \n3 \n\u0000क\u0000त\u0000 म\u0000 देय  तथा \n45 \n\u0000\u0000तशत क\u0000 दर से संग\u0000णत धनरा\u0000श।\n \n \nउपयु\u0000\u0000त के आलोक म\u0000 यह अन ुमान लगाया जा सकता है \u0000क वीडीआईएस \n1997 \nक\u0000 तुलना म\u0000 आईडीएस \n2016 \nअ\u0000धक सफल रह\u0000 है।\n \n \n(\nड\n.)\n \nसरकार ने काले धन का पता लगाने के \u0000लए नी\u0000तगत \nपहल\u0000 और \u0000वत\u0000न कार\u0000वाई के मा\u0000यम से कई \nउपाय \u0000कए ह\u0000। इन उपाय\u0000 म\u0000 शा\u0000मल है\n-\n \n(\ni)\n \nमाननीय उ\u0000चतम \u0000यायालय के दो पूव\u0000 \u0000यायधीश\u0000 क\u0000 अ\u0000य\u0000ता और उपा\u0000य\u0000ता म\u0000 \u0000वशेष जांच दल का गठन।\n \n(\nii\n) \n\u0000वदेश म\u0000 जमा काले \nधन के म ु\u0000दे से \u0000वशेष \u0000प से \u0000न\nब\nटने के \u0000लए \n“\nकाला\n \nधन\n(\nअघो\u0000षत \u0000वदेशी आय और \nप\u0000रसंप\u0000\u0000याँ\n) \nऔर कर अ\u0000धरोपण अ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\n, \n2015\n, \nजो\n \n\u0000क \n1\n.\n7\n.\n2015 \nसे लागू हुआ\n, \nका अ\u0000ध\u0000नयमन।\n \n\n(\niii)\n \nपनामा पेपर ल\u0000क मामले म\u0000 हाल  ह\u0000 क\u0000 जानकार\u0000 क\u0000 जांच पड़ताल करने के \u0000लए म\u0000ट\u0000 एज\u0000सी \u0000ुप का गठन \nकरना िजसम\u0000 क \u0000 \u0000\u0000य \u0000\u0000य\u0000 कर बोड\u0000\n, \nभा\nरतीय \u0000रजव\u0000 ब\u0000क\n, \n\u0000वत\u0000न \u0000नदेशालय और \u0000व\u0000\u0000य आस ूचना एकक के \nअ\u0000धकार\u0000 ह\u0000।\n \n(\niv)\n \nदोहरे कर प\u0000रहार करार\n/ \nकर सूचना आदान\n-\n\u0000दान करार\n/ \nबहुप\u0000ीय कंव\u0000शन के अंतग\u0000त स ूचना के आदान\n-\n\u0000दान \nको सुगम बनाने और बढ़ाने के  आशय से \u0000वदेशी सरकार\u0000 के साथ पूव\u0000 स\u0000\u0000य \u0000प से जु\nड़ना।\n \n(\nv)\n \nनॉन इं\u0000\u0000सव उपाय\u0000 पर \u0000यान क \u0000 \u0000\u0000त करते हुए \u0000वदेश म\u0000 जमा काले धन से संबं\u0000धत मामल\u0000 पर और \u0000भाव \nवाले मामल\u0000 को \u0000ाथ\u0000मकता द\u0000 गई है ता\u0000क कर अपवंचन\n/ \nकाला धन के \u0000व\u0000\u0000ध \u0000व\u0000वसनीय \u0000नवारकता के \u0000लए \nयथाशी\u0000 उ\u0000लंघनकता\u0000ओं को अ\u0000भयोिजत \u0000कया जा सके।\n \n(\nVi\n) \nअ\u0000य बात\u0000 के  साथ\n-\nसाथ सूचना के \u0000वतः आदान\n-\n\u0000दान \nके संबंध म\u0000 बह ुप\u0000ीय स\u0000म \u0000ा\u0000धकार\u0000 करार म\u0000 \nशा\u0000मल होने तथा \u0000वदेशी लेखा कर अनुपालना अ\u0000ध\u0000नयम के अंतग\u0000त यूएसए के साथ सूचना के आदान\n-\n\u0000दान करक े \nकर अपवंचन\n/ \nकाले धन से \u0000नबटने के \u0000लए पूव\u0000 स\u0000\u0000य \u0000प से \nवैि\u0000वक \u0000यास\u0000 को और आगे बढ़ाना।\n \n(\nVii)\n \nअ\u0000य देश\u0000 के साथ डीट\u0000एए के साथ प ुनः समझौता करना ता\u0000क सूचना के आदान\n-\n\u0000दान संबंधी आ\u0000ट\u0000कल को \nअंतरा\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000य मानक\u0000 के अन ु\u0000प बनाया जा सके तथा \u0000व\u0000भ\u0000न \u0000े\u0000ा\u0000धका\u0000रताओं के साथ नए डीट\u0000एए और ट\u0000आईईए \nपर ह\u0000ता\u0000र करते हुए भारत के सं\u0000ध नेटवक\u0000 को बढ़ाना ता\u0000क स ू\nचना के आदान\n-\n\u0000दान को सुगम बनाया जा सके \nऔर पारद\u0000श\u0000ता लाई जा सके।\n \n(\nviii)\n \n\u0000व\u0000 अ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\n, \n2015 \nके मा\u0000यम से \nधन आशोधन \u0000नवारण अ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\n, \n2002 \nको संशो\u0000धत करते हुए देश \nके भीतर\n \nअथवा देश के बाहर\n, \nजहाँ संप\u0000\u0000 ल\u0000 गई है\n/ \nअपराध का \u0000\u0000तफल हुआ है\n,\n \nके समतु\u0000य मू\u0000य क\u0000 स\n\u0000प\u0000\u0000 \nक\u0000 कुक\u0000 और ज\u0000ती को समथ\u0000 बनाना।\n \n(\nix)\n \nबेनामी लेनदेन \n(\n\u0000नषेध\n) \nअ\u0000ध\u0000नयम\n, \n1988 \nको संशो\u0000धत करने के  \u0000म म\u0000 बेनामी लेनदेन \n("}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |56", "t": "Ex-Servicemen Contributory Health Scheme", "head": "LOK SABHA  \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 56 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016  \n \n PROGRAMMES BROADCASTED IN GRAMSET \n \n56. SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE:  \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING be pleased to state:\n  \n(a) The details of amount spent on Gramset, State -wise particularly in Adivasi \ndistricts during the last three years, till date;   \n(b) the details of programmes broadcasted under this scheme;  \n \n(c) whether the Government will include the Adivasi population in these \nprogrammes to promote the Adivasi culture;  \n \n(d) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(e)  if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STAT E IN THE MINISTRY OF  INFORMATION AND \nBROADCASTING [COL RAJYAVARDHAN RATHORE (Retd.)] \n  \n \n(a) to (e)  :  \nDoordarshan and All India Radio do not provide service through Gramset.  \n \n***** \n \n  \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |57", "t": "Allowances to Govt. Employees", "head": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.57 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON NOVEMBER 16, 2016 \n \nSLUMS AROUND GOVERNMENT COLONIES \n \nNo. 57   SHRI RAMESH BIDHURI: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether number of slum dwellers and shanty tenements are \nincreasing near several prominent CPWD Government colonies in \nNational Capital Region Delhi;   \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) the steps being taken by the Government to check the \nuncontrolled increase in the number of slums and slum dwellers; \n(d) whether there is any concrete and time bound scheme toremove \nthese illegal encroachments, and to rehabilitate the displaced \npeopld ; and  \n(e) if so, the details thereof and the reason for continued presence \nofslum clusters despite the schemes? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n( RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n(a) : There is no increasing trend in the number of slum dwellers and \nshanty tenements near CPWD Government colonies in National \nCapital Region Delhi.   \n(b): Does not arise. \n(c): Watch and ward measures have been put in place to avoid new \nencroachment. \n(d): Yes, Madam \n(e): The rehabilitation schemes for slum dwellers have been finalized \nby Government of National Capital Territory of Delhi (GNCTD). \nDelhi Urban Shelter Improvement Board (DUSIB) has been \nrequested to rehabilitate the existing slum dwellers.  DUSIB has \nconducted biometric survey at several locations.  Central Public \nWorks Department (CPWD) has released the payment as per \ndemand raised by DUSIB.   \n******\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |58", "t": "e-Governance in Health Sector", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nDEPARTMENT OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 58\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016\nE-GOVERNANCE IN HEALTH SECTOR\n*58. SHRI ASHWINI KUMAR CHOUBEY:\nWill the Minister of HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE be pleased to\nstate:\n(a) whether the Government is implementing e -Governance so as to keep a track on\nhospitals, doctors and patients and if so, the details thereof and including the reasons\ntherefor;\n(b) whether the Government proposes to have centralized patient data through\ne-Governance system so as to track patients details online for their medical history;\n(c) if so, the details thereof; and\n(d) the time by which the said system is likely to be implemented?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF HEALTH AND FAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI JAGAT PRAKASH NADDA)\n(a) to (d):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House\n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 58* FOR 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016\na) Yes. Government is using e-Governance by assigning “National identification\nnumber” to each healthcare facility in country and by seeding Adhaar Number of\npatients in Unique Health Identification No. (UHID) generated through “Hospital\nInformation System” applications being implemented in hospitals for automation\nof processes to facilitate internal workflow management in public hospitals\n(District Hospital, Community Health Centres) for better delivery of services to\npatients and improvement in efficie ncy of processes of hospitals. “Health\nManagement Information System” and “ Meraaspataal” application have been\nimplemented for monitoring of healthcare services delivery at public\nhospitals/healthcare facilities and to obtain patient feedback respectively.\nb) Yes\nc) A scheme to set up an ‘Integrated Health Information Platform (IHIP) ’, to\ncreate the Electronic Health Records (EHRs) of patients in a centralized manner\nand to be made available nationwide online for medical history, with the help of\nHealth Information Exchange, has been approved and is being implemented.\nd) IHIP will be implemented in a phased manner. In Phase I, IHIP will be\nimplemented on a pilot basis in two States, two Central Government Hospitals,\nAIIMS Delhi and one private hospital by 2017. On successful implementation of\nthe pilot phase, IHIP will be rolled out pan-India.\n******"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |59", "t": "Norms of Bank Branches", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 59\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016\n \n \nIMPLEMENTATION OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT\n \n \n59. SHRI VIRENDER KASHYAP\n:\n \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP be \npleased to state:\n \n \n(a) \n \nwhether implementation of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship is going \nahead successfully;\n \n \n(b) \n \nif so, the details thereof; \n \n \n(c) \n \nwhether there are States who are not implementing this scheme or are otherwise \nusing funds provided to these State; and \n \n \n(d) \n \nif so, the details thereof and the response of the Government thereon?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE \nMINISTRY OF\n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP\n \n(SHRI RAJIV PRATAP RUDY)\n \n \n(a) \nto (d) \n \nT\nhe vision of the \nSkill India \nis to fulfill the gro\nwing need for skill manpower \nacros\ns sectors and narrow the existing gap between demand and supply of skills with a\n \ntarget of skilling 104\n \nmillion\n \nfresh entrants to workforce\n \nby 2022\n, in addition to upskilling\n \n/reskilling approximately 298 million amongst those already in workforce\n. The \nMinistry\n \nof \nSkill \nDevelopment\n \nand \nEntrepreneurship\n \n(MSDE)\n \nalong with\n \n21 other Minist\nries\n \n/\n \nDepartments had achieved \ntotal skilling of 1.04 crore persons in 2015\n-\n16, which is \n36.8% more than that in 2014\n-\n15. In addition, t\nhere \na\nre \na number of \nschemes\n \nfor skilling \nbeing implemented \ndirectly \nby \nthe \nS\ntates\n, which is not part of the central compilation \nreferred to above. Further, some amount of skill development is also done by the \nindustry especially for their\n \nown workforce. The States have been implementing these \nschemes with varied degree of success, with\n \nfew performing much better than others. \nHowever, Pradhan\n \nMantri\n \nkaushal\n \nVikas Yojana (PMKVY), which is the flagship \nprogramme of skilling \nwas directly implemented by MSDE through the National Skill \ndevelopment Corporation\n(NSDC)\n. \nFurther,\n \nthe \nGovernment ha\ns decided to skill one\n \ncrore \npersons\n \nwith an outlay of \nRs\n. \n1\n200\n0\n \ncrore over a period\n \nof 4 years form 2016\n-\n17 \nto 2019\n-\n20\n \no\nut of which \n25% of the financial target will be implemented through \nthe \nStates \nand \nUTs \namounting t\no\n \nan allocation of Rs.3000 crores \nand\n \nremaining through the \nNSDC. \n \n \n**\n****\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |6", "t": "BPOs in Rural Areas", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA  \nMINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.6    \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nINDIANS STRANDED IN IRAQ \n \n6.  SHRI PRABHAKAR REDDY KOTHA: \n \nWill the Minister of EXTERNAL AFFAIRS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether some Indian workers are stranded in Erbil in Iraq as their \nvisa has lapsed and if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether any representation has been received by the Ministry in \nthis regard and if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) the steps being taken by the Government to rescue the Indians \nand bring them back to India?   \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EXTERNAL AFFAIRS \n(SHRI M. J. AKBAR) \n \n(a)  Yes. As reported by the Indian Consulate, Erbil, Iraq, 55 Indian \nworkers were stranded in Erbil, Iraq, as their visas had lapsed. This ha d \nhappened because their employers did not renew their visas and \nresidency permits. As per local rules effective from March 2016, any \nindividual who has overstayed the visa c an exit Kurdistan only after \npayment of a penalty of US$ 800/- per month for the period of overstay.  \n \n(b)  The Indian Consulate in Erbil has recently received \nrepresentations from the stranded Indian nationals  and an NGO from \nTelengana.  \n \n(c)  The Consula te had approached the host Government for \nrepatriation of these Indian nationals who have over -stayed their visas. \nThe issue was taken up by the Consul General during his meetings with \nthe Prime Minister and the Interior Minister of Kurdistan. As a result of \nthese efforts, a group of 19 Indian nationals has travelled back to India \non November 10, 2016, without payment of any overstayal penalty. The \nConsulate is also contacting the remaining 36 individuals to reconfirm \ntheir consent to be repatriated to Indi a so that the host Government \nmay be requested to facilitate their repatriation. \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |60", "t": "Manufacturing of Warships", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 60 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nOLD COACHES \n \n60.    SHRI INNOCENT: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a) whether old coaches that have outlived their utility, are widely \ndeployed in express trains across the country, posing a major \nsafety issue; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the total number of coaches \nwhich are more than twenty years old and are still being \ndeployed in trains, zone-wise; \n \n(c) the reasons for delay in replacement of old coaches; and \n \n(d) the corrective steps taken by Railways in this regard? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n (SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a)  to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n\n--2/- \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 60 BY SHRI INNOCENT TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARDING OLD \nCOACHES  \n \n(a):  No, Madam. Passenger coaches that have outlived their utility \nare not deployed in expre ss trains. The prescribed codal life of ICF \n(Integral Coach Factory) type of coaches is 25 years and that of LHB \n(Linke Hofmann Busch) type of coaches is 35 years. Replacement of \ncoaches on age-cum-condition basis is a continual process. \n \n(b): As per the h olding of coaches as on 31.03.16, the number of \ncoaches more than 20 year old that are still being deployed in \ntrains, zone-wise, is as under: \nZonal railway Number of coaches which are more \nthan twenty years old and deployed \nin trains \nCentral Railway 718 \nEastern Railway 757 \nEast Central Railway 375 \nEast Coast Railway 223 \nNorthern Railway 821 \nNorth Central Railway 183 \nNorth Eastern Railway 232 \nNorth Frontier Railway 228 \nNorth Western Railway 239 \nSouthern Railway 752 \nSouth Central Railway 591 \nSouth Eastern Railway 458 \nSouth East Central Railway 98 \nSouth Western Railway 423 \nWestern Railway 536 \nWest Central Railway 105 \nTotal 6739 \n\n-2- \nAll these coaches are within the prescribed codal life of 25/35 years \nas mentioned in (a) above. \n \n(c): Does not arise.  \n \n(d): Replacement of old coaches by new coaches are done regularly \non case to case basis depending upon condition and codal life of old \ncoaches. This is an on-going exercise. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |61", "t": "Enrolment of Girl Students", "head": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n  \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION No. 61 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 \n \nEnrolment of Girl Students \n \n†*61 SHRI PARBHUBHAI  NAGARBHAI VASAVA: \n  SHRI ARVIND SAWANT: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n   \n(a) whether a large number of parents in rural ar eas are unable to send their children to \nschools particularly girls and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) the ratio of girl child to total children enrolled in rural areas, State/UT-wise; \n \n(c) the estimated proportion of tota l education budget re leased/utilised in this regard during \nthe last three years including current year, year-wise and State/UT-wise; \n \n(d) whether the Government provides nutritious food  to adolescent girls and if so, the details \nthereof, State/UT-wise; and \n \n(e) the steps taken/proposed to be taken by the G overnment to ensure enrolment of each girl \nchild in the schools? \n \n \nA N S W E R \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n(a) to (e) : A statement is laid on the Table of the House \n \n \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 61 TO BE ANSWERED ON 21 ST NOVEMBER,  2016 \nREGARDING “ ENROLMENT OF GIRL STUDENTS” ASKED BY SHRI  \nPARBHUBHAI NAGARBHAI VASAVA, SHRI ARVIND SAWANT \n \n(a) & (b): The enrolment of children in schools is captured under Unified District \nInformation System for Education (U-DISE) which s hows that the percentage of girls enrolled is \nincreasing every year in rural areas both at th e elementary level and secondary level. The \nnational level figures are given below:-  \nYear Elementary level (I-VIII) Secondary level (IX – X) \n2010-11 48.64 45.02 \n2015-16 48.75 47.73 \nSource U-DISE \n There is very small gap between the percen tage of girls and boys enrolment in both the \nurban and rural areas at elementary, secondary and higher secondary level. A table showing the \nsame is at Annexure. \n(c): The estimated proportion of total budget released for the e ducation of girls in the last \nthree years including the current year is as below: \n(In Crores) \nSr. No. Budget Released 2014-15 2015-16 2016-17 \n1 Department of School \nEducation and Literacy \n13609.25 12472.07 12565.80 \n2 Department of Higher \nEducation \n6376.22 7446.34 8016.21 \nTotal 19985.47 19918.41 20582.01 \n The State / UT wise fi gures are not available. \n \n\n \n \n(d):  Under Mid-day Meal Scheme being impl emented by the Ministry  of Human Resource \nDevelopment, central financial assistance is being provided to all States and UTs for \nimplementation of the scheme. Under the Sche me, all States and UTs are providing mid-day \nmeals to children, including adolescent girls, studying in Classes I to VIII of Government, \ngovernment aided, Special Traini ng Centres and Madrasas and Maqtabs supported under Sarva \nShiksha Abhiyan. \nSome State Governments like Andhra Prades h, Karnataka, Tamil Nadu and Telangana \nand Union Territory Administrations like Puducherry and Lakshadweep are providing mid-day \nmeals to children studying in classes IX, X and XII also, from their own resources. \n The Government of India, Ministry of Woman & Child Development is implementing \nRajiv Gandhi Scheme for Empo werment of Adolescent Girls  - Sabla , a Centrally-sponsored \nscheme in 205 districts selected fr om all the States/UTs. The scheme  aims at all-round \ndevelopment of adolescent girls(AGs) of 11-18 years (with a focus on all out-of-school AGs).   \nThe scheme has two major components: Nutrition and Non Nu trition Component. \nNutrition component aims at improving the hea lth and nutritional status, the non nutrition \ncomponent addresses the developmental needs of adolescent girls. Under the Nutrition \ncomponent of the scheme, the out of school A dolescent Girls in the age group of 11-14 years \nattending AWCs and all girls in the age group of 14-18 year s are provided Supplementary \nNutrition containing 600 calories, 18-20 grams of protein and micr onutrients @ Rs. 5/ \nbeneficiary/day for 300 days in a year. The Nutriti on is given in the form of Take Home Ration \n(THR) or Hot Cooked Meals. In th e Non Nutrition Component, out of school adolescent girls of \n11-18 years are  provided Iron and Folic Acid (I FA) supplementation, health check-up & referral \nservices, nutrition & health educ ation, ARSH counseling/guidance on family welfare, life skill \neducation, guidance on accessing public services and vocational training (only 16-18 year old \nadolescent girls).   \n(e): Universal enrolment is the first goal  of Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan, a programme for \nuniversalisation of elementary education and all efforts are being made to bring all children \nincluding girls to school. SSA has provided 2.04 lakh primary and 1.59 upper primary schools \n\n \n \nfor ensuring universal access.  SSA  strategies for promotion of gi rls education include inter-alia, \nopening of school"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |62", "t": "Basic Infrastructure in Schools", "head": " \n \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION AND LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 62 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21ST NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nBasic Infrastructure in Schools \n \n*62. SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether there is lack of basic infrastructure  and staff in the Government and private schools \nand if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether some students are reportedly st udying in porta cabin-like classrooms with \nprefabricated structures and tin roofs in the Government schools in some States and if so, the \ndetails thereof and the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the Government has assessed the total number of students in each school and \navailability of the infrastructure, inter-alia, furniture, desks, etc., in schools, if so, the details \nthereof, State/UT-wise and if not, the reasons therefor;  \n \n(d) whether the Government proposes to take acti on against schools devoid of the infrastructure \nand teaching staff and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and  \n \n(e) the funds sanctioned/released/spent for the above-mentioned purposes, during each of the last \nthree years and the current year, State/UT-wise and year-wise? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI PRAKASH JAVADEKAR) \n \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 62 FOR 21.11.2016 REGARDING BASIC INFRASTRUCTURE IN \nSCHOOLS ASKED BY SHRIMATI KOTHAPALLI GEETHA. \n  \n(a): Yes, Madam.   \n Details on shortage of basic in frastructure in government a nd private schools at elementary \nlevel as per latest Unified District Information System for Education (U-DISE) data are as under:   \nLevel Drinking \nWater Ramp Boundary \nWall Playground Library \nGovernment \nNumber of \nSchools \nlacking \nfacilities \n37,236 6,47,601 4,42,637 4,85,190 1,60,929 \nPercentage \nof Schools \nlacking \nfacilities \n3.46% 60.13% 41.10% 45.05% 14.94% \nPrivate \nNumber of \nSchools \nlacking \nfacilities \n1 2,10,260 32,205 55,766 60,092 \nPercentage \nof Schools \nlacking \nfacilities \n0.00% 78.45% 12.02% 20.81% 22.42% \n \n About 13.58 crore children in  11.08 lakh government sc hools have access to gender \nsegregated toilets. Under Swachh Vidyalaya initi ative, 4,17,796 toilets were  constructed in 2,61,400 \nelementary and secondary government schools in  a period of one year from 15.8.2014 to 15.8.2015, \nthus ensuring that every government school has sepa rate functional toilets fo r girls and boys.  States \nand UTs have been instructed to ensure that a ll the schools in respective State/UT, including those \nunder the non-Government sector (p rivate, aided schools etc.) should  have provision for separate \ntoilets for boys and girls; and safe and adequate drinking water facilities to all children, in accordance \nwith the norms under Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act, 2009. \n  There are 51,81,791 sanctioned posts of te achers, out of which 42,74,206 teachers are in-\nposition and 9,07,585 vacancies (17.51%) at elementary level under State and Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan \n(SSA) as on 31.3.2016. State/UT-wise details are at Annexure–I.  There are 24.87 lakh teachers in \nprivate schools at elementary level. \n\n \n \n \n Details on shortage of basic infrastructure and staff in government  and private schools at \nsecondary level are at Annexure–II. \n(b): Status of Porta Cabin/Pre-Fabricated Structures Sanctioned under SSA is as under: \nS. No. States Year of Sancti ons Sanctioned Achievements \n1.  Chhattisgarh \n2007-08 48 (500 seater Porta \nCabin Schools) \n48 (500 seater \nPorta Cabin \nSchools) \n2010-11 40 (500 seater Porta \nCabin Schools) \n40 (500 seater \nPorta Cabin \nSchools) \n2016-17 113 Pre-Fab ACRs Yet to be started \n2.  Rajasthan 2007-08 111 Pre-Fab ACRs 111 \n \n Ministry of Human Resource Development ha s sanctioned one Additional Class Room (ACR) \nfor Class IX in 58 porta cabins Upper Primary Sc hools (UPS), in the year 2015-16 to the State of \nChhattisgarh.  The Government of Chhattisgarh, in its proposal for the year 2016-17 surrendered the \nACR for Class IX of 58 porta cabins and propos ed for regular upgradation of the 60 UPS upto \nsecondary level. In the year 2016-17, 25 upper pr imary schools running in porta cabins which were \nfound eligible, have been approved for upgradation to secondary schoo ls as per the proposal of the \nState Government, alongwith requisite infrastructure.   \n(c) & (d): The Central Government supports St ate Governments and UT  Administrations for \ncreation and augmentation of infr astructural facilities in govern ment elementary and secondary \nschools under Sarva Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA) and Rashtriya Madhyamik Shiksha Abhiyan (RMSA) \nprogrammes.  The  requirement of  infrastructural facili ties in schools are worked out every year by \nthe respective Sta"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |63", "t": "Jagdishpur-Haldia Gas Pipeline Project", "head": "LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 \n \nJAGDISHPUR-HALDIA GAS PIPELINE PROJECT  \n \n* 63.     KUNWAR BHARATENDRA:   \n             SHRI MOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO: \n      \n \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS be pleased to state: \n \nisVªksfy;e vkSj izkd`frd xSl ea=h \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to finance the gas grid network from Jagdishpur -Haldia-\nBokaro-Dhamra gas pipeline project to push gas supply to eastern region, if so, the details \nthereof;  \n \n(b) the benefits likely to accrue to various States therefrom along with the details of funds made \navailable and utilised for laying the said gas pipeline Project, agency and State/UT-wise;  \n \n(c) whether the said project proposes to connect the eastern part of the country with the National \nGas Grid network and if so, the details thereof and the time by which the work on the said gas \npipeline is likely to be started; and  \n \n(d) the status of the project along with the further steps taken to expedite the execution of the \nproject? \nANSWER \n \nपेट्रोलियम और प्राकृलिक गैस मंत्रािय में राज् य मंत्ररी (स् विंत्र प्राार  \n(श्ररी धमेन्‍द र प्रधान  \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) IN THE MINISTRY OF \nPETROLEUM & NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) to (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 63 ASKED BY KUNWAR BHARATENDRA AND SHRI \nMOHITE PATIL VIJAYSINH SHANKARRAO,  MPs TO BE ANSWERED ON \nNOVEMBER 21, 2016 \n(a): Yes, Madam. The Government of India has taken a decision to provide a capital \ngrant of Rs.5176 crore (i.e. 40% of the estimated capital cost of Rs.12,940 Crore) to GAIL \nfor development of Jagdishpur -Haldia/Bokaro-Dhamra Gas Pipeline (JHBDPL) project, \npopularly known as the “Pradhan Mantri Urja Ganga” of Eastern India. This project will \nensure the availability of clean and eco -friendly fuel, i.e. natural gas to the Eastern part of the \ncountry. The approved year-wise capital grant details are as under:   \n \nYear Amount (Rs. Cr.) \n2016-17 900 \n2017-18 1200 \n2018-19 1500 \n2019-20 1576 \nTotal 5176 \n \n(b): JHBDPL will ensure the supply of Natural Gas to the industrial, commercial, domestic \nand transport sectors in the States of Uttar Pradesh, Bihar, Jharkhand, Odisha and West \nBengal. The details of the districts and the villages of these States to be covered by JHBDPL \nproject are as under: \n \nState Districts \ncovered \nVillages \ncovered \nPipeline \nlength \n(Km) \nAnticipated \nCost \n(Rs. Cr.) \nUttar Pradesh 8 402 342  1200  \nBihar 9 439 441  2200 \nJharkhand 11 339 524  2540 \nOdisha 13 568 762  4000 \nWest Bengal 8 523 550  3000 \nTotal 49 2270 2619  ~ 12,940   \n \nThis Capital Grant will encourage the supply of eco -friendly fuel at affordable tariffs to \nindustries and will encourage industrial development in these states. Further, GoI has decided \nsimultaneous development of City Gas Distribution (CGD) networks in ci ties namely \nVaranasi, Patna, Ranchi, Jamshedpur, Bhubaneswar, Kolkata, Cuttack etc. en -route of the \nproject. It will bring clean cooking fuel at the door step of Domestic households as well as \nprovide clean fuel to transport sector in the eastern region.  Government had earlier approved \nrevival of three Fertilizer Units (i.e. FCIL - Gorakhpur, HFCL - Barauni and FCIL -Sindri) \nalong the route of this pipeline project. On revival, these units will be the major gas customers \nfor this pipeline project. GAIL is the project implementing agency of this pipeline project and \nthe Capital Grant of Rs 5,176 Crore  will be provided to GAIL only. This Grant  will be met \nthrough the Cess collection under the Oil Industry Development Act, 1974.  So far GAIL has \n\nmade the financial commitment of Rs.1493 crore for the development of JHBDPL project in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar.  \n(c): Yes Madam, the JHBDPL project would connect the eastern part of the country with \nthe National Gas Grid.  GAIL has already co mmenced the construction activity in the State of \nBihar (Patna & Barauni Section) on September 15, 2015. The entire pipeline project is \nscheduled to be completed by December, 2020.  \n \n(d): This project implementing agency, i.e. GAIL has completed the survey  work for the \nentire project. In order to acquire the Right of User (RoU) land for pipeline development in \nthe State of Uttar Pradesh and Bihar, Government has published the notification for about 755 \nKm under Section 3(i) and 425 Km under Section 6(i) und er Petroleum & Mineral Pipelines \n(PMP) Act, 1962. Awards for all major supplies (line pipes, line material etc.) and laying \nworks for Phulpur to Dobhi(Gaya) and Dobhi to Patna/Barauni section  completed. GAIL \ncommenced the construction work on 15 th September 2015 on Patna & Barauni Section in the \nState of Bihar. About 41 km welding work and 19 km of pipeline lowering work completed so \nfar in this section. Further, the construction work in the S"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |64", "t": "Closed Tea Gardens", "head": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON NOVEMBER 16, 2016 \nDANGEROUS GOVERNMENT QUARTERS \n \nNo. 64   SHRI HARINARAYAN RAJBHAR: \n \nWill the Minister of URBAN DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) whether the Central Public Works Department (CPWD) has \ndeclared a number of Government \nquarters/residences/bungalows/flats as dangerous;   \n(b) if so, the details thereof State-wise including Uttar Pradesh; \n(c) the reasons for the poor maintenance of these Government flats; \nand \n(d) the steps taken by the Government to renovate these \nGovernment residences in a phased manner? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF URBAN DEVELOPMENT \n(RAO INDERJIT SINGH) \n \n(a) & (b):  Yes, Madam.  State-wise details are annexed. \n \n(c) & (d):  Most of the flats are very old and require extensive repairs.  \nQuarters are renovated in a phased manner wherever \nfeasible.  Some colonies are taken up for redevelopment.               \n   \n****** \n  \n\nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (B) OF LOK \nSABHA UNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 64 FOR 16.11.2016 \nREGARDING “DANGEROUS GOVERNMENT QUARTERS”. \n \nSTATE WISE DETAILS OF QUARTERS/ RESIDENCES / \nBUNGALOWS / FLATS DECLARED AS DANGEROUS BY CPWD \n \nSl.No. Name of States No. of Govt. Quarters/Bungalows \netc. \n1 Delhi 1228 \n2 Maharashtra 660 \n3 Tamil Nadu 52 \n4  Goa 40 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 10 \n6 Himachal Pradesh 36 \n7 Chandigarh 02 \n8. Gujarat 100  \nIn addition 6 class rooms, 3 labs \nand 12 single room of 80 bedded \ngirls dormitory at Roop Nagar, \nBharuch) \n9. West Bengal  40 \n10. Uttar Pradesh Nil \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |65", "t": "Unemployment", "head": "  GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LAW AND JUSTICE \nLEGISLATIVE DEPARTMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 65 \n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON WEDNESDAY, 16th NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nVOTING OPTION BY NRIs \n \n65. SHRI RAJESHBHAI CHUDASAMA \n \n   Will the Minister of LAW AND JUSTICE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has finalised the system to cast vote through voting \noption by Non-Resident Indian (NRI) voters; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) the time by which is likely to be implemented/notified? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LAW AND JUSTICE AND ELECTRONICS \nAND INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY \n(SHRI P.P.CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a)to ( c) At present, under the provisions of section 20A of the Representation \nof the People Act, 1950 read with the Conduct of Election Rules, 1961, NRI \nvoters can cast their vote in person in the constituency where their names are \nregistered. However, b ased on the recommendation of the Election \nCommission, a proposal is under consideration of the Government to introduce \nproxy voting and postal ballot including e -postal ballot system for overseas \nelectors. e -Postal ballot  envisages transmission of blank postal ballot paper \nelectronically and thereafter return of the same by post. "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |66", "t": "Memorial on Morarji Desai", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nDEPARTMENT OF ATOMIC ENERGY \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 66 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nPRODUCTION OF ATOMIC ENERGY  \n \n66. DR. RAMESH POKHRIYAL \"NISHANK\": \n SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR:  \n \nWill the PRIME MINISTER be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the current production of Atomic energy in the country and the target fixed therefor \nfor the next ten years; \n  \n(b) whether it is more economical in comparison to other power/energy and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(c) the strategy adopted to ensure the safety and s ecurity of the Atomic energy stations; \n \n(d) the countries with which agreements have been c oncluded to boost research and \ndevelopment in the field of Atomic energy; and \n \n(e) the steps taken to promote capacity building an d skill development in the field of \nAtomic technology in the country? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR PERSONNEL, PUBLIC GRIEVANCES & PENSIONS AND \nPRIME MINISTER’S OFFICE (Dr. JITENDRA SINGH): \n \n(a) The generation of electricity from nuclear powe r in the current year (2016-17) upto \nOctober 2016 has been 22347 MUs. The target for the  current year is 36000 MU. \nTargets for generation are finalised on an annual b asis. So the targets for next ten \nyears have not been fixed. \n \n(b) Nuclear power tariffs in India are comparable t o those of other contemporary base \nload electricity generating plants. \n \n(c) Nuclear power plants are sited, designed, const ructed and operated to the highest \nsafety standards. Nuclear power plants are designed using principles of redundancy, \ndiversity and adopting a defence-in-depth approach,  constructed to highest quality \nstandards and operated strictly in line with approv ed procedures by trained and \nlicensed personnel. There is also a robust regulato ry mechanism in place. The \noverall philosophy of security and the principles a nd procedures governing the \nfunctioning of the security units in nuclear power plants are laid down in the AERB \nmanual on nuclear security. The security surveillan ce / monitoring at the nuclear \npower plant stations in the country is carried out by the Central Industrial Security \nForce (CISF). \n \n (d) Some of the major countries with which agreeme nts have been concluded to boost \nresearch and development in the field of Atomic Ene rgy are USA, Russia, France, \nUK, Australia, Republic of Korea, Canada and Czech Republic. \n \n \n(e) DAE has established dedicated multi-discipline capacity building and skill \ndevelopment centers at multiple locations in the fi eld of nuclear science and \ntechnology.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |67", "t": "Shortage of Doctors/Staff in ESI Hospitals", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION  NO. 67 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nNARROW GAUGE LINES \n \n67.  SHRIMATI RAKSHATAI KHADSE: \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to at least do the regular \nmaintenance of the locomotive, coaches and track so as to \nrender the services keeping in view the safety issue and if \nso, the details thereof;  \n \n(b) whether the Government proposes to convert these narrow \ngauge lines to broad gauge; and    \n \n(c) i f so, the time bound programme chalked out in this regard \nincluding for Pachora - Jamner in Central Railway, Mumbai \nZone? \n \n ANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n       (SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a)  Yes, Madam.  \n(i) Regular preventive maintenance is carried out for \nrendering satisfactory service of diesel locomotives to \nensure safe train operation.  \n(ii)  Regular maintenance of all the coaches (including Narrow \nGauge coaches) is done as per the prescribed schedules \nkeeping in view the safety and passenger amenities. \n.…2/- \n \n\n: 2 : \n \n(iii) Maintenance of track is a regular activity.  Maintenance \nand  inspection of track is done as per laid down \nprocedures.  The defects noticed during inspections get \nrectified in the planned manner.  If considered necessary, \nsuitable speed restrictions are imposed by field officials \ntill rectification of defect is done. \n \n(b) Conversion of Narrow Gauge (NG) lines, wherever feasible, \nand of Meter Gauge (MG) lines to Broad Gauge (BG) ha s been \ntaken up by Indian Railways, as a part of Uni -gauge policy in \nphases, depending on overall availability of funds and relative \npriority of the route. \n \n(c)   Survey for Gauge Conversion of Pachora -Jamner line and \nextension to Malkapur (104 Km) has been included in Rail \nBudget 2016-17 and survey taken up by Central Railway. \n \n               ***** \n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |68", "t": "Promotion of Agro-Based Cottage Industries", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \nLOK  SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 68 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF NEW RAILWAY LINES \n \n \n68.      SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN: \n                     \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state:   \n \n \n(a) whether the Railways has received proposals from the \nGovernment of Gujarat for construction of new railway lines, \ngauge conversion of the existing lines and doubling of tracks to \ncope with the movement of goods from ports and industrial \ntownships to the large hinterland; and  \n \n(b) if so, the action taken so far to implement the sanctioned work, \nif any, and towards sanctioning of remaining work, proposal -\nwise?    \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) & (b): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n*****    \n \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 68 BY SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN  TO \nBE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARDING \nCONSTRUCTION OF NEW RAILWAY LINES  \n \n(a) & (b): Requests for new lines, gauge conversion and doubling, \nboth formal as well as informal, are received by Railways at various \nlevels i.e. Railway Board, Zonal Railways and Divisional \nHeadquarters, etc. As receipt of such requests/suggestions is a \ncontinuous and dynamic process, centralized compendium of such \nrequests is not maintained. However, in recent past Government of \nGujarat has suggested certain works, the details of which are \nappended. \n \nTwo new lines, eight gauge conversion and nine doubling  \nprojects covering a length of 363 km., 1467 km and 984 km and \ncosting ` 3766 crore, ` 6510 crore and ` 6477 crore respectively \nfalling fully/partly in the State of Gujarat have been sanctioned \nwhich also will help in development of ports and industries. O n \nthese projects, an expenditure of ` 4359.47 crore has been incurred \nupto March, 201 6, with an outlay of ` 3670 crore for the yea r 2016-\n17. Besides these projects, Bhimnath-Dholera (28 km)  new line \nproject has also been included in the Budget 2016 -17 subj ect to \nrequisite approvals from the Government.      \n \nCompletion of these projects is dependent upon many factor s such \nas land acquisition, statutory clearances like forestry and wild life \nclearances, shifting of services, cutting of trees, construction of  \nroad over bridges and road under bridges by road maintaining \nagencies, apart from availability of adequate funds. Since many of \nthese factors are beyond the control of Ministry of Railways, \ntimelines for completion of all the projects are not feasible to be \nfixed.  \n***** \n \n\n \nAPPENDIX REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTON NO. 68 BY SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN  TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 16.11.2016 REGARDING CONSTRUCTION OF NEW \nRAILWAY LINES  \n \n(a)  & (b):  Details and status of works suggested  by Government of \nGujarat in the recent past are as under:   \n \nS.No. Subject Status \n  New Line   \n1 Provision of \nadequate funds for \nnew line between \nSomnath to Kodinar \nfor development of \nChhara Port \nSomnath to Kodinar new line has been added \nto Rajkot - Veraval gauge conversion project \nas material modification. The main project of \ngauge conversion has already been \ncompleted. An outlay of ` 50 crore has been \nprovided for this project for the year 201 6-\n17. Land acquisition has been taken up. \nTender for major bridges is under \nfinalisation. The allotment of funds for the \nyear 2016-17  is  sufficient in present stage \nof land acquisition for the project.  \n2 New Railway line \nBhavnagar-Adhelai-\nDholera-Vataman-\nPetland (Survey \nproposed)  \n Bhavnagar-Adhelai-Dholera-Vataman-\nPetland: Survey for Bhavnagar to Tarapur \nNew Line via Dholera, has been completed. \nCost of this line has been assessed as ` 745 \ncrores with RoR of ( -) 1% and Planning \nCommission has not agreed to the proposal. \n3 Dholera-Bhimnath \n(Survey proposed)  \nThe work included in the Budget 2016 -17 \nsubject to requisite approvals from the \nGovernment.   \n4 Khambhat to \nKhambhat Port \n(Survey proposed)  \nKhambhat to Khambhat Port:  Survey for this \n20 Km line was sanctioned in 2013 -14 but \nGujarat Maritime Board has info rmed that \nKhambhat port will not be developed due to \nthe construction of Kalpsar Dam at location \nof Khambhat Port.  \n \n…..2/- \n \n\n-2- \n \n  Gauge Conversion   \n1. Gauge conversion \nof existing MG/NG \nrail line \nAhmedabad-Botad-\nBhavnagar. \nBotad-Bhavnagar is already a  broad gauge \nsection. Gauge conversion of Ahmedabad -\nBotad has been taken up at an anticipated \ncost of ` 567 crores. An expenditure of          \n` 75 crore has been incurred upto March, \n2016. An outlay of ` 102 crore has been \nprovided for this project for th e year 201 6-\n17. Final Location Survey , earthwork, \nbridges work and station building work have \nbeen taken up.    \n Doubling   \n1 Bhruch-Samni-\nDahej \nGauge conversion of this section has been \ncompleted and commissioned. A"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |69", "t": "Promotion of Wildlife and Forest Tourism", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*69 \nANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 \n \nPROMOTION OF WILDLIFE AND FOREST TOURISM  \n \n*69. SHRI RAMDAS C. TADAS:  \nSHRI NANA PATOLE:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether th e Government plans to develop wildlife and forest \ntourism in the country, if so, the details thereof along with its \nscope in various States, State/UT-wise including Maharashtra;  \n(b)  whether the Government has received any proposals in this \nregard from th e various State Governments or public \nrepresentatives and if so, the details thereof and the status of \nthe said proposals;  \n(c)  the funds allocated for the purpose during the last three years \nand the current year, year-wise;  \n(d)  the other steps taken by  the Government to develop these \nforests as tourist sites; and  \n(e)  the time by which these places are likely to be developed \nunder wildlife and forest tourism?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a)  to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n \n******** \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*69 \nANSWERED ON 21.11.2016 REGARING PROMOTION OF WILDLIFE \nAND FOREST TOURISM. \n \n(a) to (d): India has huge tourism potential including wildlife an d \nforest tourism in the country including in the State of Maharashtra. \nDevelopment and promotion of tourist destinations and products \nincluding Wildlife & Forest Tourism is primarily the responsibility of \nthe respective State Government/Union Territory (UT ) \nAdministration. \n \nHowever, for development of tourism infrastructure in the \ncountry, the Ministry of Tourism has launched the Swadesh Darshan \nscheme- Integrated Development of Theme -Based Tourist Circuits, \nin 2014-15.  \n \nWildlife Circuit has been identifie d as one of the thirteen \nthematic circuits for development under this operative scheme.  \n \nThe Ministry has sanctioned following projects in the year \n2015-16 for the Wildlife Circuit under Swadesh Darshan scheme:  \n \nState Name of Project Amount \nSanctioned \n(Rs. in Crore) \nMadhya \nPradesh \nDevelopment of Wildlife Circuit at Panna - \nMukundpur- Sanjay- Dubri-Bandhavgarh-\nKanha-Mukki-Pench \n92.22 \nAssam Manas-Pobitora-Nameri-Kaziranga-Dibru-\nSaikhowa as Wildlife Circuit in Assam  \n95.67 \n \n(e): The completion period of pro jects sanctioned under the \nSwadesh Darshan scheme varies from 18 to 36 months.  \n******** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |7", "t": "Vulgartity in TV Programme", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16/11/2016  \n  \nVULGARTITY IN TV PROGRAMME \n \n*7.  SHRI  JANARDAN SINGH SIGHRIWIL : \n \nWill the Minister of INFORMATION AND BROADCASTING    \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government has taken cognizance ris e in  obscenity, vulgarity and \nnudity in the television programmes in the country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details of channels against whom act ion has been taken for violating the \nnorms/guidelines during the last three years and the current year; \n \n(c)  whether there is any self regulation in place to check/curb vulgarity and indecency in \nprogrammes telecast on TV channels and if so, the details in the this regard; and  \n \n(d) the steps taken/being taken by the Government t o monitor the content of the \nprogrammes being  telecast on Doordarshan and Private channels? \n  \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF INFORMATION & BROADCASTING \n(SHRI M. VENKAIAH NAIDU) \n \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n \n********** \n \n\n \nSTATEMENT AS REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 7 FOR ANSWER ON 16.11.2016  \n \n \n(a) to (d):  As per existing regulatory framework, all programmes telecast on TV \nchannels are required to adhere to the Programme Co de  prescribed  under the Cable \nTelevision Networks (Regulation) Act, 1995 and Cabl e Television Network Rules, 1994 \nframed thereunder.  The Act does not provide for pr e-censorship of any programme \ntelecast on such TV channels.  However, it prescrib es that all programmes telecast on such \nTV channels should be in conformity with the prescr ibed Programme Code enshrined in the \nsaid Act and the rules framed thereunder, which con tains a whole range of parameters to \nregulate programmes including content of obscenity,  vulgarity and nudity in TV \nprogrammes.  \n \nMinistry has constituted an Inter Ministerial Commi ttee (IMC) to look into the \nviolations suo-motu or whenever violation of the Pr ogramme and Advertising Codes is \nbrought to the notice of this Ministry in respect o f private satellite TV channels by vigilant \ncitizens about objectionable content on TV. IMC has  representatives from the Ministry of \nHome Affairs, Defence, External Affairs, Law, Women  and Child Development, Health and \nFamily Welfare, Consumer Affairs and a representati ve from the industry in Advertising \nStandards Council of India (ASCI). IMC meets period ically and recommends action in \nrespect of violations. Details of action taken on v iolation of Programme Code by private TV \nchannels for telecast of content of obscenity, vulg arity and nudity in TV programmes during \nthe last three years and the current year are enclosed at Annexure. \n \nTV channels are required to preserve a copy of thei r telecast for 90 days. In case a \nviolation is reported they are obliged to share the  recordings and archive it until the matter \nis resolved.  \n \nGovernment has encouraged self-regulation in electr onic media by the Industry. \nNews Broadcasters Association (NBA), which represen ts Private television news and \ncurrent affairs broadcasters, as part of its self-r egulation mechanism, has formulated  a  \nCode  of  Ethics  and  Broadcasting  Standards  covering  a  wide range of principles to self-\nregulate news broadcasting. NBA has also formulated  News Broadcasting Standards \nRegulations. They have set up a Two-Tier structure to deal with content related complaints- \nat Tier I, by the individual broadcasters and at Ti er II, by News Broadcasting Standards \n\nAuthority (NBSA). The Authority consists of a Chair person who is a retired Judge of the \nSupreme Court and eight other members. Members of t he Authority comprise of 4 (four) \neminent editors employed with broadcaster and 4 (fo ur) persons having special knowledge \nand/or practical experience in the field of law, ed ucation, medicine, science, literature, \npublic administration, consumer affairs, environment, human psychology and/or culture.  \n           \nBesides, Indian Broadcasting Foundation (IBF), whic h represents non-News and \nentertainment channels, has laid down Content Code & Certification Rules 2011 covering \nan entire gamut of content-related principles and c riterion for television broadcast.  As part \nof self-regulation mechanism, a two-Tier complaints  redressal system has been set up by \nIBF. At the Tier-I level, each Broadcaster has set up a Standard and Practices (S&P) \nDepartment with a Content Auditor to deal with the   complaints   received for content aired \non its channels.  At the Tier II, a Broadcast Conte nt Complaints Council (BCCC) has been \nset up. The BCCC has 13 Members headed by a retired  Judge of the Supreme Court or \nHigh Court as Chairperson and 12 other Members, viz. 4 eminent persons, 4 members from \nany National Level Statutory Commissions and 4 Broa dcast members and two (2) Special \nInvitees to deal with complaints against regional langua"}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |70", "t": "Import of Metallic Scrap", "head": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMIINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 70 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \n   CHARGES FOR USING URINALS \n \n70.    DR. KIRIT SOMAIYA: \n      Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether a charge of Re.1 has been imposed to use urinals in Mulund \nand other railway stations in Mumbai suburban railways;  \n \n(b)     if so, the details and reasons therefor;  \n \n(c)    whether the Government is aware that commuters have raised strong \nobjections against this charge and has demanded its withdrawal;  \n \n(d)    if so, whether the Railways will consider to withdraw this charge; and \n \n(e)    if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) to (b):  Yes, Madam.  A charge of `1 has been imposed to use urinals in \n‘Pay & Use’ toilets at Mulund and other suburban railway stations  in \nMumbai in order to provide better and hygienic services at sub urban \nstations having high foot fall.  However, for toilet b locks which are \nmaintained departmentally, there is no usage charge. \n \n(c): Amongst 22 stations where urinals are being charged at  `1, \ncomplaints have been received for 3 stations namely Mumbai CST, Mulund \nand Shahad station. \n \n(d) & (e) : As per extant polic y guidelines of Zonal Railway, urinals are \nbeing charged for `1 at Mumbai suburban railway stations. No such \nproposal for revision of policy guidelines is in pipeline at present.  \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |71", "t": "Development of Salt Industry", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \nDEPARTMENT OF INDUSTRIAL POLICY & PROMOTION \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 71. \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, THE 21ST NOVEMBER,  2016. \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF SALT INDUSTRY \n \n*71.  SHRI KUNDARIYA MOHAN BHAI KALYANJI BHAI: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY be pleased to state: \n                            वाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ं ्री \n(a)  whether meetings were held between  Government of Gujarat and Union  \nGovernment in 2012, in connection with  development of salt industry and \nagarias in the State and if so, the outcome of the meetings; \n \n(b)  the action taken/being taken to  reimburse the State Government the  \nexpenditure incurred on development of  salt industry schemes/projects and \nwelfare schemes for the salt workers; and \n \n(c)  whether the Union Government  proposes to contribute 50 per cent amount  of \nthe State Salt Projects so that more  projects and better activities are taken up  \nin Gujarat and if so, the details thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nवाणिज्‍ य‍वव ‍द्यग ‍ााज्‍ यं ्री‍स्‍‍ वतं ्‍्रभााा(स्रींतंरी‍िरंमलाा‍ीरीतंाांि(‍ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nOF THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(SHRIMATI NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a): No meeting was held between Government of Gujarat and Government \nof India in 2012 regarding development of salt industry and agarias in \nthe State. \n \n(b): There is no scheme of the Government of India which envisages \nreimbursement to the State Government of the expenditure incurred on \ndevelopment of salt industry/projects and welfare schemes for salt \nworkers. \n \n(c):  No such proposal is under consideration. \n \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |72", "t": "Pradhan Mantri Ujjwala Yojana", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 72 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nGAUGE CONVERSION \n \n \n †72.  SHRI RAHUL KASWAN: \n \n \n \nWill the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n \n(a)  the number of gauge conversion projects sanctioned, completed \nand lying incomplete in the country during the last three years \nalong with the complete details thereof; \n  \n(b)  the number of gauge conversion projects in the State of Rajasthan \nwhich  have been completed after sanction and those lyin g \nincomplete; \n  \n(c)  whether in this year's budget, provision had been made for the \ncompletion of gauge conversion work in the State of Rajasthan and \nif so, the details thereof, project-wise; \n  \n(d)  whether work has stated for the sanctioned amount and the time by \nwhich it will be completed; and \n  \n(e)  if so, the details thereof?  \n  \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n \n(a) to (e):   A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( e) OF UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 72 BY SHRI RAHUL KASWAN TO BE ANSWERED IN LOK SABHA \nON 16.11.2016 REGARDING GAUGE CONVERSION \n \n(a):   Four Gauge Conversion projects have been included in Railway Budgets \nsince 2013-14 subject to requisite approvals.  Details are as given below:- \nS. \nNo. \nRly State Project Year Length      \n(in km)  \nLatest \nCost  \nOutlay \n2016-\n17  \n(in ` Crore) \n1 NER UP Indara-Dohrighat (34 \nKm) \n2016-17 34 120 0.02 \n2 NER UP Bahraich-Mailani incl \nbyepass at Mailani \n(230 Km) \n2016-17 230 1900 0.02 \n3 WR GUJ Ahmedabad- \nMahesana (70 Km) \n2015-16 70 420 100 \n4 SECR MAH Nagbhir-Nagpur (106 \nkm) \n2013-14 106 401 25 \n \nIn three financial years starting from 2013 -14, a total of 2337 Km Gauge \nConversion has been completed.  As on date, 39 Gauge Conversion works have \nbeen taken up. \n \n(b) to (e):  One gauge conversion project viz. Suratpura-Hanumangarh (174 Km) \nhas recently been completed  falling fully/partly in the State of Rajasthan .  \nDetails of ongoing gauge conversion projects falling fully or partly in the State of \nRajasthan are as under:- \nS. \nNo. \nRly. State Project Name Year of \nSanction \nLength \n(in \nKm) \nCost  Expendi-\nture \nupto \n31.03.16 \nOutlay \n2016-\n17 \n(In ` Crores) \n1 NCR MP, \nRAJ \nGwalior-\nSheopurkalan with \nextension to Kota \n(284 km) \n2010-11 284 3845 10.46 35 \n\nS. \nNo. \nRly. State Project Name Year of \nSanction \nLength \n(in \nKm) \nCost  Expendi-\nture \nupto \n31.03.16 \nOutlay \n2016-\n17 \n(In ` Crores) \n2 NCR RAJ Dholpur-Sirmuttra \nwith extension to \nGangapur City \n(144.6 km) \n2010-11 144.6 2530 35.66 50 \n3 NWR RAJ Sadulpur-Bikaner \n& Ratangarh-\nDegana (394.35 \nkm) with \nRatangarh-\nSardarshahar (44 \nkm) sanctioned as \nMM \n2007-08 438.35 886.\n22 \n814.14 10 \n4 NWR RAJ, \nHAR \nJaipur-Ringus-\nChuru & Sikar-\nLoharu (320.04 \nkm) \n2008-09 320.04 915 453.54 100 \n5 NWR RAJ Ajmer-Chitturgarh-\nUdaipur incl MM \nUdaipur-Umra and \nMavli-Bari \nSadri(393 Km) \n1996-97 393 865 557.18 15 \n6 WR RAJ, \nGUJ \nAhmedabad-\nHimmatnagar-\nUdaipur including \nModasa-Shamlaji \nRoad(22.53Km) \n2008-09 321.73 1662 233.69 675.25 \n \nThus a total allotment of `885.25 Crore has been made for these Gauge \nConversion projects.  As  execution of a railway project  requires several \nclearances and assistance from other departments which are beyond the control \nof railways, it will not be feasible to fix time lines for completion of all the \nprojects.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |73", "t": "Beedi Workers", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 73 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n \nHIGH SPEED RAIL PROJECT \n \n73.        SHRI A. ARUNMOZHITHEVAN: \n  \n     Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether a Joint Committee has held talks with Japanese authorities \nvery recently regarding India’s ambitious high speed rail project;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c) whether India has requested for drawing up of a sche dule of project \nimplementation and appointment of a General Consultant before \nfinalisation of the loan agreement for the said project; and \n \n(d) if so, the response received from the Japanese authorities in this \nregard? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n(SHRI RAJEN GOHAIN) \n \n(a) & (b): Yes, Madam. Third Joint Committee meeting under the \nchairmanship of Vice Chairman, NITI Aayog was held with Japanese \ncounterpart on 7th October, 2016 to review the progress of Mumbai -\nAhmedabad High Speed Rail project.     \n \n(c) & (d) : Yes, Madam. Both Government of India and Government of \nJapan have agreed to the schedule of implementation of project and \nappointment of the General Consultant before finalisation of loan \nagreement.  \n***** "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |74", "t": "Maintenance of Heritage Sites by Private Sector", "head": "1\n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF CULTURE \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n74\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON \n21.11.2016\n \nKARTIKA 30\n, 193\n8\n \n(SAKA)\n \n \n \nMAINTENANCE OF HERITAGE SITES BY PRIVATE SECTOR \n \n \n \n*74.\n \nSHRI  R. GOPALAKRISHNAN:\n \nSHRI  HARISH CHANDER \nALIAS\n  \nHARISH DWIVEDI: \n \n \nWill the Minister of CULTURE be pleased to state:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe number of historical monuments and heritage sites maintained by the \nArchaeological Survey of India (ASI) State/UT\n-\nwise; \n \n(b)\n \nwhether heritage sites in the country are being given to private compa\nnies for \ntheir renovation and maintenance and if so, the details thereof and the reasons \ntherefor; \n \n(c)\n \nthe other steps taken by the Government to promote private sector’s \ninvolvement in heritage promotion along with the details thereof; and \n \n(d)\n \nwhether\n \nASI has undertaken responsibility of maintaining historical/heritage \nsites situated in foreign countries also and if so, the details thereof?\n \n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE, CULTURE AND TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)\n \n \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA)\n \n \n \n(a)to(d)\n \nA Stateme\nnt is laid on the table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n\n2\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) TO (\nd\n) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.\n74\n \nFOR \n21.11.2016\n \n \n \n(a)\n \nThe State\n-\nwise list of 3686 monuments/sites \nmaintained by the \nArchaeological Survey of India in the countr\ny \nis at Annexure. \n \n \n(b)\n \nAs on date, Archaeological Survey of India has undertaken conservation \nand development of Humayun’s Tomb, Delhi in collaboration with Aga \nKhan Trust for Culture (AKTC) and conservation and development of \nTomb of Mohammed Shah known\n \nas Mubarak Shah’s Gumbad, Delhi in \ncollaboration with Indian National Trust for Cultural Heritage (INTACH). \nFurther MOU’s have been signed with State Governments for \nmaintenance and upgrading visitor facilities.  However, in no case whole \nwork is entruste\nd to any private company. \n \n(c)\n \nArchaeological Survey of India has issued an Expression of Interest on \nPublic Private Partnership Module (PPP) for providing World class \nfacilities at the important tourist visited monuments/sites.  Under this \nExpression of \nInterest (EOI) 20 different services which includes web\n-\nbased information and other innovative ideas which enhance the \npopularity of the monument and bring it at par have been offered.  \n \n(d)\n \nOn request from MEA the ASI has taken up conservation work of Ta\n \nProhm Temple in Combodia, Vat Phom temple in Lao PDR and Anande \nTemple in Myanmar.\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n3\n \n \nANNEXURE \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 74 FOR 21.11.2016\n \n \nNUMBER OF CENTRALLY PROTECTED MONUMENTS/SITES UNDE\nR THE JURISDICTION \nOF ARCHAEOLOGICAL SURVEY OF INDIA IN THE COUNTRY \n \n \n \nSl.No.\n \nName of State\n \nNos. of Monuments\n \n1\n.\n \n \nAndhra Pradesh\n \n129\n \n2\n.\n \n \nArunachal Pradesh\n \n03\n \n3\n.\n \n \nAssam\n \n55\n \n4\n.\n \n \nBihar\n \n70\n \n5\n.\n \n \nChhattisgarh\n \n47\n \n6\n.\n \n \nDaman & Diu (U. T.)\n \n12\n \n7\n.\n \n \nGoa\n \n21\n \n8\n.\n \n \nGujarat\n \n203\n \n9\n.\n \n \nHaryana\n \n91\n \n10\n.\n \n \nHimachal Pradesh\n \n40\n \n11\n.\n \n \nJammu & Kashmir\n \n69\n \n12\n.\n \n \nJharkhand\n \n13\n \n13\n.\n \n \nKarnataka \n \n506\n \n14\n.\n \n \nKerala\n \n28\n \n15\n.\n \n \nMadhya Pradesh\n \n292\n \n16\n.\n \n \nMaharashtra\n \n285\n \n17\n.\n \n \nManipur\n \n01\n \n18\n.\n \n \nMeghalaya\n \n08\n \n19\n.\n \n \nMizoram\n \n01\n \n20\n.\n \n \nNagaland\n \n04\n \n21\n.\n \n \nN.C.T. Delhi\n \n174\n \n22\n.\n \n \nOdisha\n \n79\n \n23\n.\n \n \nPuducherry (U.T.)\n \n07\n \n24\n.\n \n \nPunjab\n \n33\n \n25\n.\n \n \nRajastha\nn\n \n162\n \n26\n.\n \n \nSikkim\n \n03\n \n27\n.\n \n \nTelangana\n \n08\n \n28\n.\n \n \nTamil Nadu\n \n413\n \n29\n.\n \n \nTripura\n \n08\n \n30\n.\n \n \nUttar Pradesh\n \n743\n \n31\n.\n \n \nUttarakhand\n \n42\n \n32\n.\n \n \nWest Bengal\n \n \n136\n \n \nTOTAL\n \n3686\n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|STARRED   |75", "t": "Fund for Start-up Companies", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED  QUESTION NO.  75  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 16.11.2016 \n  \nONGOING RAIL PROJECTS IN UP \n \n  +  75.   SHRI KAUSHAL KISHORE:     \n  \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS  be pleased to state t he details of \nrail projects in Uttar Pradesh through which employment \nopportunities may be/have been