en Carbide Balls for \nPinaka Warhead  \nvi. Automatic Detonator Filling Plant (Rs. 11 Crore) at Ammunition Factory, \nKhadki ( AFK) – for modernization of facility for production of \nDetonators \n \n    Proposed investment in the ordnance factories for Financial Year 2016 -17 \nis Rs. 1461.42 Crore (RE). \n ……2/- \n\n:  2  : \n \n \n(c)  Export of arms, ammunition and weapon systems by Ordnance Factory \nBoard (OFB) is being done in accordance with broad guidelines laid for export \nto foreign countries using spare capacity after meeting the Services ’ \nrequirements and compliance to country -specific instructions issued by Ministry \nof External Affairs (MEA) from time to time. \n \nThe details of exports of weapons and other equipment planned for 2016 -\n2017 country-wise are as under: \n \nYear Country Nature of Items Value of \nOrder (USD) \nValue of \nExport(INR) \n2016-17 \n(Planned) \nIndonesia General Stores & \nClothing \n2,36,700 Exported  \nRs. 8.38 \nCrore \n(upto Nov’16) Mauritius Medium caliber \nweapon \n10,45,742 \nMaldives Small Caliber \nAmmunition \n1,10,250 \nUzbekistan General Stores & \nClothing \n3,785 \n Germany Small Caliber \nAmmunition \n8,800 \nKenya Large Caliber \nAmmunition & \nSignaling Smoke  \n10,45,048 \nItaly Large Caliber \nWeapon \n28,22,962 \nTotal  Planned Value of Export in 2016 -17  \n(USD). \n52,73,287  \n \n****** \n\nANNEXURE-I  REFERRED IN THE REPLY GIVEN IN THE STATEMENT  IN \nPART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 347 FOR ANSWER ON \n9.12.2016 \n \n*Value of Turnover for Last Two Years & Current Year   \n(Including Issues to Sister Factories)                          In Rs. Crore  \nSl. \nNo. Factory 2014-15 2015-16 2016-1 7 \n(upto   03/12/2016) \nAmmunition & Explosives (AE) Division \n1 Ammunition Factory, Khadki 896.04 901.48 486.85 \n2 Cordite Factory, Aruvankadu 154.39 185.78 128.47 \n3 High Explosives Factory, Khadki 193.39 231.86 128.69 \n4 Ordnance Factory Khamaria 1410.40 1848.23 473.64 \n5 Ordnance Fa