ON 16TH NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nGROWTH OF INDIA POST \n \n35. SHRI SISIR KUMAR ADHIKARI: \n \nWill the Minister of COMMUNICATIONS be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  whether the express mail service of India Posts has doubled its revenue during \nthe last three years; \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c)  the steps taken to maintain and augment the growth of business of India Posts; \n \n(d)  whether the Government proposes to increase the limit of single/joint deposits \nscheme in Monthly Income Plan to develop the business growth of India Posts; and \n \n(e)  if so, the details thereof and the action taken in this regard? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (IC) OF THE MINISTRY OF COMMUNICATIONS & \n MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n(SHRI MANOJ SINHA) \n \n \n(a) & (b)  Department of Posts provides the services of Speed Post, Express \nParcel and Business Parcel for express delivery of letters and parcels.  Revenue \nperformance of Speed Post and Express/Business Parcel during the last three years \nis given at Annexure ‘A’. \n \n(c) Following steps have been taken to maintain and augment the growth of \nbusiness of Department of Posts: \n \n The Parcel booking and handling facilities have been upgraded to cater \nto the increasing eCommerce market.  \n Parcel handling capacity has been augmented by establishment of 57 \nintegrated Parcel Processing Centres and mechanising the \npickup/delivery of parcels.  \n Cash - on - Delivery facility especially for e -commerce companies has \nbeen provided as a value addition  to the Speed Post and \nExpress/Business Parcel.  \n Online Track and Trace system for Speed Post has been strengthened. \nIn addition to the website of the Department of Posts \n(www.indiapost.gov.in), the status of an article can also be tracked \nthrough an android based mobile application. \nContd…2.- \n \n\n \n  \n \n \n \n-2- \n \n The facility of Short Messaging Service (SMS) has been provided for \ngiving the delivery status of an article. \n National Account facility has been introduced under Speed Post and \nExpress/ Business Parcel for contractual customers. \n Provision has been made for packaging, shrink -wrap facilities, secure \nplastic seals at selected locations.  \n Application Programme Interface (API) has been provided to the \ncontractual customers for real time information.  \n  Same day/ next day delivery of eCommerce articles in select cities has \nbeen started. \n Railway tickets are being sold through post offices under an agreement \nsigned with the Ministry of Railways. Presently this service is available \nin 343 post offices across India.   \n Government of India has introduced Sovereign Gold Bond scheme \n(SGB) in the Union Budget 2015 -16. During the six tranches issued in \nlast and current financial year, 96215 Sovereign Gold Bond applications \nfor Rs.81.40 crore were collected through Post Offices across the \ncountry. \n Department has started distribution of Gangajal sourc ed from Gangotri \nand Rishikesh through Post Offices as well as online through ‘ePost \nOffice’.  \n Philately stamps are also sold online through ‘ePost office’. \n Department of Posts in association with Ministry of Agriculture has \nstarted distribution of high yi elding seeds and dissemination of \ninformation on new farm technologies to farmers through the village \nPost Offices in 14 states. \n Tie ups have been made with Railway Recruitment Boards, CBSE and \nvarious universities/institutions etc for collection of their examination fee \nthrough Post Offices. \n Information technology based Core Insurance Solution has been  \nimplemented for Postal Life Insurance and Rural Postal life Insurance \nleading to customer friendly initiatives such as online premium payment, \nSMS alerts for premium due etc. \n \n(d) & (e) As of now, there is no proposal under the consideration of the \nGovernment for increasing the limit of deposit for single/joint account under the Post \nOffice Monthly Income Scheme. \n \nContd…3/- \n \n  \n\n \n  \n \n \n \n \n-2-   \nAnnexure-A \n \nInformation of revenue Generated by Speed Post,  \nExpress /Business Parcel  for last three years  \n \n Speed Post Express/Business Parcel \nYear Revenue \n (Rs. In crore) \nPercentage \ngrowth \n in revenue \nRevenue \n (Rs. In crore) \nPercentage \ngrowth \n in revenue \n2013-14 1372.21 8.78 % 77.63 -1.57 % \n2014-15 1495.21 8.96 % 112.47 44.88 % \n2015-16 1605.25 7.04 % 149.00 33.32 % \n \n \n************* "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |350", "t": "WTO Ruling against DCR Norms", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 350 \nANSWERED ON FRIDAY THE 9TH DECEMBER, 2016 \n[AGRAHAYANA 18, 1938(SAKA)] \n \n \nINTERNATIONAL COMPETITION NETWORK \n \nQUESTION \n \n*350.  DR. PRITAM GOPINATH MUNDE: \n          SHRI ANANDRAO ADSUL: \n   \nWill the Minister of CORPORATE AFFAIRS                           कारपोरेट कार्य मंत्री \nbe pleased to state: \n \n(a)   whether the Competition Commission of India (CCI) has been set \nup to prevent practices having adverse effects on competition and \nto promote and protect interest of consumers and ensure freedom \nof trade carried on by other participants in markets in India and if \nso, the details thereof; and  \n \n(b)  whether CCI has proposed to host the 2018 International \nCompetition Network Annual Conference and if so, the details \nthereof? \n \n \nANSWER \n \n \nTHE MINISTER OF CORPORATE AFFAIRS                  (SHRI ARUN JAITLEY) \n                 कारपोरेट कार्य मंत्री                                             (श्री अरुण जेटली) \n \n \n(a) & (b) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n******* \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN ANSWER TO LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 350 FOR 09.12.2016 REGARDING INTERNATIONAL \nCOMPETITION NETWORK \n \n \n(a) Yes, Madam.  The Competition Commission of India (CCI) promotes \ncompetition and enhances consumer welfare through its orders.  It prevents \npractices having adverse effects on competition and abuse of dominance \nby enterprises. It has passed cease and desist  orders and also imposed \npenalty in several cases where violation of Competition Act have been \nnoticed.   \n \n(b) The International Competition Network (ICN) has accepted the \nproposal of the CCI to host the ICN Annual Conference 2018 in New Delhi.    \n \n***** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |351", "t": "Development of Land Bank and Waterfront", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SHIPPING \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.351 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 17TH NOVEMBER, 2016 \nDEVELOPMENT OF LAND BANK AND WATERFRONT \n351.  KUNWAR HARIBANSH SINGH:  \nSHRI S.R. VIJAYAKUMAR:  \nSHRI ASHOK SHANKARRAO CHAVAN:  \nSHRI SUDHEER GUPTA:  \nDR. SUNIL BALIRAM GAIKWAD:  \nSHRI T. RADHAKRISHNAN:  \nSHRI BIDYUT BARAN MAHATO:  \n \nWill the Minister of SHIPPING be pleased to state: \nपोतप�रवहनमंत् \n(a)  whether the Government proposes to develop Mumbai Port Trust's huge land bank and \nwaterfront; \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n(c)  whether any Committee has been set up for the purpose and if so, the details and the \ncomposition thereof;  \n(d)  whether the Committee has submitted its report and if so, the details thereof indicating \nmajor recommendations made by the Committee; and  \n(e)  action taken by the Government on the said recommendations?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF SHIPPING  \n (SHRI PON RADHAKRISNAN) \n \n(a): Yes , Madam. Mumbai Port proposes to develop its land and water front. \n \n(b): Mumbai Port has about 752 HA of land in Mumbai city and its nearby areas.  Out of this \nabout 200 HA are used for port operations. About 500 HA of land is proposed to be developed \nwith a mix of port operations, business, office, commercial, retail, entertainment, community \nprojects and convention centres, etc.  The proposed projects would also include renewable \nenergy and waste water recycling, creation of spaces for community recreation and engagements, \nmaritime museum, marinas etc. Mumbai Port has already invited global tender from eligible \nnational/international consulting firms for “Appointment of Consultant for Planning, Design and \nProgram  Management  Support for Master Planning and Infrastructure Design of the Mumbai \nPort”.  \n \n(c)to(e):Government of India had set up a Committee under Chairmanship of Smt. Rani Jadhav  \nfor preparing a road map for development of Port’s water front and land.  The Committee has \nsubmitted the report.  The report is under examination in the Ministry of Shipping. \n \n***** \n\n \n \n \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |352", "t": "Construction of NH from Mumbai to Goa", "head": " \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LO K \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 352 FOR ANSWER ON 9.12.2016 \n \n \n \n(a) to (c): No specific MoUs on Maritime Surveillance have been entered \ninto.  However, Government has approved exchange of white shipping \ninformation with various countries.  Pursuant to that, Technical \nAgreements have already been signed in this regard with Australia, USA, \nVietnam, Maldives, Oman and Seychelles.  These Agreements will enable \ngreater Maritime Domain Awareness. \n \n******* \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |354", "t": "Construction of Projects on Mahanadi River by Chhattisgarh", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF WATER RESOURCES, \nRIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA REJUVENATION \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 354 \nANSWERED ON 17.11.2016 \n \nCONSTRUCTION OF PROJECTS ON MAHANADI RIVER BY CHHATTISGARH \n \n354.  SHRI BHARTRUHARI MAHTAB \nWill the Minister of WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT AND GANGA \nREJUVENATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government of Odisha has raised certain objections to the Union Government on the \nprojects being constructed by the Government of Chhattis garh across Mahanadi river in the recent past; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the action taken/being taken by the Union Government to address \nthe said objections so far;  \n(c) whether the Government of Chhattisgarh has violated any norms of the A greement of 1983 signed \nbetween the two States; \n (d) if so, the details thereof and the reasons therefor along with the action taken/ being taken by the \nUnion Government to restore such violated terms and conditions of the said agreement; and \n (e) the mechanism developed by the Union Government to ensure adherence to the terms and conditions \nof the agreement by the States sharing river water or to avoid river disputes across the country along \nwith the other steps taken/being taken by the Government in this direction? \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR WATER RESOURCES, RIVER DEVELOPMENT & GANGA \nREJUVENATION  \n(DR. SANJEEV KUMAR BALYAN) \n \n(a)&(b) The Government of Odisha had raised certain objections over construction of barrages, \n&reservoir structures taken up by Chhattisgarh.  An Inter State meeting was held on 29/07/2016 chaired \nby Officer on Special Duty (OSD) to MoWR, RD & GR with the Chief Secretaries of the two States, to \nresolve the issues. Subsequently, a meeting was chaired  by Minister MoWR, RD & GR with Chief \nMinisters of concerned States on 17/09/2016 to resolve water resources issues/Projects in Mahanadi \nBasin between the two States. \n(c) to (e)   In the inter -State meeting of 19/09/2016, it was decided to form a Special Committee as well \nas an Expert Committee, as suggested by Govt. of Odisha.  The Ministry constituted two Teams from \nCWC (one for each State) to  visit and list out the water resources project in Odisha and Chhattisgarh \nthose have been constructed or are under construction without the approval of Technical Advisory \nCommittee (TAC) of MoWR,RD &GR. While relevant information from Chhattisgarh has been \nreceived, information from Odisha has not been received. \n This Ministry vide letter dated 22.09.2016 has sent the proposed composition of Expert Committee for \nsuggesting measures for monitoring the issues on Mahanadi, Term of Reference were sent to \nGovernment of Odisha and Chhattisgarh for t heir consent. Government of Chhattisgarh has nominated \nthe representative for the Expert Committee. A reminder dated 8.11.2016 was also sent to Government \nof Odisha, however, the response of Government of Odisha has not been received.  \n***** \n\n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |355", "t": "Promotion and Use of Renewable Energy Sources", "head": " \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 355 FOR ANSWER ON \n9.12.2016 \n \n \n(a) A five year (2015 -2020) Long Term Roll on Works Plan \n(LTRoWP) for 519 roads of length 22225.17 km as identified by \nArmy has been approved for construction/improvement by Border \nRoads Organisation (BRO) in the border regions of the country.  \nState-wise details of the roads are enclosed as Appendix-A.  \n \n(b) & (c): No, Madam. Based on the requirement of the Army, at \npresent there is no proposal to extend the operations of BRO in \nother States. \n \n \n******** \n \n \n\nAPPENDIX  ‘A’  REFERRED IN THE REPLY GIVEN IN THE \nSTATEMENT IN PART (a) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 355 FOR ANSWER ON 9.12.2016 \n \n \n \nSTATE WISE ROADS ENTRUSTED TO BRO IN THE \nCOUNTRY FOR NEW CONSTRUCTION/UPGRADATION: \n \nS/No State / UT Nos of \nroads \nLength (in km) \n1 Andaman & \nNicobar \n1 23.94 \n2 Arunachal Pradesh 99 5267.51 \n3 Assam 4 100.61 \n4 Himachal Pradesh 11 924.52 \n5 Jammu & Kashmir 231 7122.47 \n6 Manipur 21 1838.00 \n7 Mizoram 11 888.44 \n8 Nagaland 10 841.18 \n9 Punjab 10 276.68 \n10 Rajasthan 53 2621.02 \n11 Sikkim 37 910.17 \n12 Tripura 2 201.04 \n13 Uttarakhand 27 1117.01 \n14 West Bengal 2 92.60 \n Total: 519 22225.17 \n \n****** \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |356", "t": "Review of Schemes for Sports", "head": 