 be pleased to state:\n(a) whether the Government proposes to establish Physiotherapy Council on the line of Medical\nCouncil of India (MCI) in order to check the quality of education in the stream;\n(b) if so, the details thereof; and\n(c) if not, the reasons therefor and the other measures/steps taken by the Government to address\nthe problem of low intake of students opting to be physiotherapists?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HEALTH AND\nFAMILY WELFARE\n(SHRI FAGGAN SINGH KULASTE)\n(a): No.\n(b): Does not arise.\n(c): Physiotherapy is a part of Allied Health and a separate Council for each discipline under\nthe broad umbrella of Allied Health is not required."}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |488", "t": "Banking Ombudsman", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF FINANCE\nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES\nLOK SABHA\nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 488\nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 18TH NOVEMBER, 2016 / 27 KARTIKA, 1938 (SAKA)\nBANKING OMBUDSMAN\nQUESTION\n488. SHRI RAOSAHEB DANVE PATIL:\n            \n Will the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state:\n(a) the number of complaints/grievances received, settled and pending by Banking Ombudsman during the last three years and the current year, \npublic and private bank-wise, State-wise;\n(b) the number of Banking Ombudsman officers appointed over the last three years and the current year;\n(c) whether the staff strength in the Banking Ombudsman is inadequate for handling the increasing number of complaints; and\n(d) if so, the details thereof along with the steps taken by the Government to improve working condition and settle the pending cases expeditiously?\nANSWER\nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE\n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR)\n (a): The information relating to number of complaints / grievances received, settled and pending (bank-wise) in Banking Ombudsman offices during \nlast three years i.e. 2013-14, 2014-15, and 2015-16 and current year relating to public and private sector banks, 