URISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)  \n(DR. MAHESH SHARMA) \n \n(a) to (c): The Ministry of Tourism has sanctioned the project \n‘Development of Heritage Circuit in Ahmedabad -Rajkot-Porbandar-\nBardoli-Dandi in Gujarat’ in 2016 -17 under the Heritage Circuit \nTheme of Swadesh Darshan Scheme for an amount of Rs.93.48 \ncrore. The major components sanctioned under the project are \nProjection mapping shows, Audio Visual shows, Exhibition Hall , \nTourist Facilitation Centre, Auditorium cum Interpretation Centres, \nWayside Amenities, Signages etc.  \n \n \n******** \n \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |738", "t": "Trade with Gulf Countries", "head": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 738 (H)  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 21st NOVEMBER, 2016 \n \nTRADE WITH GULF COUNTRIES \n738 (H). SHRI GOPAL SHETTY: \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (वाͨणÏय एवं उɮयोग मंğी ) be \npleased to state: \n(a) the details of India's trade with the Gulf countries during the last three years and the \ncurrent year;  \n(b) whether India's trade with the Gulf countries has witnessed an increase during the current \nyear;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(d)  the steps taken by the Government to enhance trade with the Gulf countries during the \nensuing five year plan period? \nANSWER \nokf.kT; ,oa m|ksx jkT; ea=h ¼Jherh fueZyk lhrkje.k½ ¼Lora= izHkkj½ \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY \n(INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SMT. NIRMALA SITHARAMAN) \n \n(a) to (c): The details of India’s trade with Gulf countries (viz. Bahrain, Kuwait, \nOman, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, UAE) during the last three years and the current year \nare at Annex- I and II. As per available DGCIS data, India’s trade with Gulf countries \nhas witnessed a decline during the current year, except in the case of Oman. \n \n(d): Trade Fairs/buyers sellers meets are regularly organized in Gulf countries under \nMarket Access Initiative (MAI) scheme of D/o Commerce with a view to \ndiversify/boost exports and enhance trade with Gulf Co-operation Council \nCountries. \n \n\n \nAnnex-I \nDepartment of Commerce \nMonthly Foreign Trade Statistics of India (Principal Commodities and Countries) Version 6.0 \nRegion-wise all countries Trade for West Asia- GCC region  \n(Period: April-March) \nS. \nNo\n. \nCountry \n2013-2014 % Growth 2014-2015 % Growth 2015-2016 % Growth \nExports Imports Total Trade Trd. Bal. Exports Impor\nts Exports Imports Total Trade Trd. Bal. Export\ns \nImpor\nts Exports Imports Total Trade Trd. Bal. Exports Impor\nts \n1    BAHARAIN  639.36 563.24 1,202.60 76.13 5.95 -15.26 472.98 446.25 919.23 26.74 -26.02 -20.77 654.14 356.9 1,011.04 297.24 38.3 -20.02 \n2    KUWAIT  1,061.14 17,153.55 18,214.69 -16,092.41 0.01 3.41 1,198.89 13,381.97 14,580.85 -12,183.08 12.98 -21.99 1,247.51 4,969.69 6,217.20 -3,722.19 4.06 -62.86 \n3    OMAN  2,812.27 2,951.18 5,763.45 -138.91 8.19 46.85 2,379.44 1,752.24 4,131.69 627.2 -15.39 -40.63 2,190.79 1,674.71 3,865.50 516.08 -7.93 -4.43 \n4    QATAR  969.06 15,707.99 16,677.04 -14,738.93 41.02 0.1 1,054.98 14,604.71 15,659.69 -13,549.74 8.87 -7.02 902.04 9,022.16 9,924.20 -8,120.12 -14.5 -38.22 \n5    SAUDI ARAB  12,218.96 36,403.65 48,622.61 -24,184.69 24.86 7.08 11,162.55 28,107.56 39,270.11 -16,945.01 -8.65 -22.79 6,394.48 20,321.33 26,715.81 -13,926.86 -42.71 -27.7 \n6    U ARAB EMTS  30,520.42 29,019.82 59,540.24 1,500.60 -15.96 -25.85 33,028.08 26,139.91 59,167.99 6,888.17 8.22 -9.92 30,290.01 19,445.68 49,735.69 10,844.33 -8.29 -25.61 \nTotal of West Asia- GCC 48,221.20 101,799.42 150,020.63 -53,578.22 -5.55 -5.82 49,296.92 84,432.63 133,729.56 -35,135.71 2.23 -17.06 41,678.97 55,790.47 97,469.44 -14,111.50 -15.45 -33.92 \n% Share in India's total 15.34 22.61             15.88 18.85             15.89 14.64             \nIndia's total 314,405.30 450,199.79 764,605.09 -135,794.49 4.66 -8.26 310,338.48 448,033.41 758,371.89 -137,694.