ese \nstudents in foreign countries; \n \n(d)  if so, the details of the countries so identified and the other changes made by \nthe Government in this regard to admission in IITs for Scheduled Caste/ \nScheduled Tribe and Persons with Disability (PWD)category candidates;  \n \n(e)  whether the Directors of IITs have op posed this move of outsourcing students \nin IITs; and \n \n(f)  if so, the reasons put forward by them and other steps taken or being taken \nby the Government for smooth conducting of admission in IITs? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(DR. MAHENDRA NATH PANDEY) \n \n(a) to (d) :  Foreign students have been allowed to register for JEE (Advanced) 2017 \nand the seats allotted to them are supernumerary with a cap of 10% of total \nnumber of seats in each course. It has also been decided to conduct JEE \n(Advanced) 2017 examination in 6 examination centres abroad, namely Addis \nAbaba (Ethiopia), Colombo (Sri Lanka), Dhaka (Bangladesh), Dubai (UAE), \nKathmandu (Nepal) and Singapore.  For SC/ST students the qualifying marks in \nthe 12th Class exam have been relaxed from 75% to 65%.  \n  \n(e) : No, Madam. \n(f) : Does not arise. \n***** \n \n\nF.No. H-11016-41/2016-TS.I \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Human Resource Development \nDepartment of Higher Education \nTechnical Section - I \n***** \n \nSubject: Lok Sabha Unstarred Question No. 764 for answer on \n21.11.2016, asked by Shri As aduddin Owaisi, regarding \nForeign Students in IITs.    \n \nMay kindly see the admitted version  of the Lok Sabha Unstarred \nQuestion No. 764, for answer on 21.11.2016, asked by Shri Asaduddin \nOwaisi, regarding Foreign Students in IITs.  The Question reads as under:  \n  \n(a)  whether the Government has deci ded to allot 10% additional seats \nto foreign students in Indian Institutes of Technologies (IITs); \n \n(b)  if so, the details thereof;  \n \n(c)  whether the Government has id entified examinations centres for \nthese students in foreign countries; \n \n(d)  if so, the details of the coun tries so identifi ed and the other \nchanges made by the Government in  this regard to admission in \nIITs for Scheduled Caste/ Sche duled Tribe and Persons with \nDisability (PWD)category candidates;  \n \n(e)  whether the Directors of IITs have opposed this move of \noutsourcing students \nin IITs; and \n \n(f)  if so, the reasons put forward by them and other steps taken or \nbeing taken by the Government for smooth conducting of \nadmission in IITs? \n \n   2. Based on the information availa ble in the Section,  a draft reply to \nthe above Question has been attemp ted and placed on the file for \nconsideration and approval of the Hon’ble MoS.  \n "}, {"k": "questions|ls|16|10|UNSTARRED |765", "t": "Steel Prices", "head": " \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.765 \nFOR ANSWER ON 21/11/2016 \n \nSTEEL PRICES \n \n765. SHRIMATI V. SATHYA BAMA: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the recent rise in prices of  steel and steel products have affected  \nproduction and supply of steel in the country; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) the total quantity and value of steel  produced and the domestic demand and  \nsupply achieved in the country during each of the last three years; and \n \n(d) the total quantity and value of st eel imported/exported during the said period,  \ncountry-wise? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE FOR STEEL         (SHRI VISHNU DEO SAI) \n \n(a) No, Madam. \n \n(b) Does not arise, in view of answer to (a) above. \n \n(c) Total quantity of Crude Steel produced, domestic demand and supply for \nFinished Steel in the country during each of the last three years are given below: \n \n(in ‘000 tonnes) \nYear Production \n(Crude Steel) \nReal consumption \n(Demand)  \n(Finished steel) \nSupply \n(Finished steel) \n2013-14 81693 74096 73684 \n2014-15 Prov) 88980 76355 79358 \n2015-16 Prov) 89776 80448 81738 \n(Sou